{"artifact_digest":"sha256:34bcb98cb518db905aecf8473f605b621b4259cc50df9a4176c34fe6a9dc44a6","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/34/34bcb98cb518db905aecf8473f605b621b4259cc50df9a4176c34fe6a9dc44a6.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:b1d56a56dde68ea21de25f1b729510be09200947018c2fcd8a9b7785b3f95347","bundle_entry_key":"bounded-corridor-branching-forces-exponential-growth","bundle_id":"population.critical-percolation-thinning-bridge-001","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"w441/bundle_001.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:probability.percolation.critical:bounded-corridor-branching-forces-exponential-growth","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Suppose the rooted b-ary tree, b>=2, admits an injective vertex map f into a locally finite graph G, and every parent-child image pair has G-distance at most a fixed L>=1. Then |B_G(f(root),Ln)|>=b^n, hence liminf_{r->infinity}|B_G(f(root),r)|^(1/r)>=b^(1/L)>1. Thus no graph of subexponential volume growth can support such an embedding.

Proof: the b^n vertices at tree-depth n are distinct images and each is within distance Ln of the root image. For arbitrary r use n=floor(r/L). This gives the liminf bound. The conclusion needs injectivity and a uniform length bound. It makes no assertion about variable-length corridors, repeated vertices, or dependent block processes.

This rules out a tempting thinning bridge that tries to find a uniformly bounded independent branching network inside every critical cluster on a subexponential graph. Such a network would already contradict ambient growth, whether or not percolation is critical.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:01f5472ebb869472b5d75049ecf42557b199c6165f836a799d663090e3d82d59","revision_digest":"sha256:00b0b4d9365e8362dc7917fcb4518a4e9097831b06854d653418bf0efc78facb","source_id":"owner:w441:P0043:2026-10-10:bounded-corridor-branching-forces-exponential-growth","source_revision":"draft-as-written-2026-10-10","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

