[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] Let $i=0,1,2,\cdots$. If a family of random variables $\{\eta_t^\epsilon\}_{0<\epsilon<1,t\geq 0}$ satisfies
  \begin{align*}
    \eta_t^\epsilon = O_{Q^\epsilon}^{T}(\epsilon^i),
  \end{align*}
  then it holds
  \begin{align*}
    \eta_t^\epsilon = O_{P}^{T}(\epsilon^i).
  \end{align*}

