[Prop Smooth of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] \begin{enumerate}	
\item[\rm(1)] Any $G$-Kato measure is smooth in the sense of Definition~(defi:smooth of the paper).
\item[\rm(2)] Any $G$-bounded measure charging no semi-polar sets is smooth in the sense of Definition~(defi:smooth of the paper). 
\end{enumerate}

[Proposition prop:r-tail-compensator-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] There exist constants \(C<\infty\) and \(c>0\) such that, for every \(n\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left(
\sup_{2^n\le\lvert\xi\rvert\le2^{n+1}}
\left(
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{pre}}_{\xi,n}
+
\sup_{L\ge1}\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,n,L}
\right)
>
2n^{-2}2^{-sn/2}
\right)
\le
C2^{-cn}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, the probabilities in (equation eq:r-tail-compensator-probability-paper of the paper) are summable in 
\(n\).

[Lemma lem:local CLT of arXiv:2412.02160, 'A functional central limit theorem for weighted occupancy processes of the Karlin model'] Fix $\epsilon\in(0,1)$. Then, there exists $C>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\max_{k\in J_{np}}\abs{\mathbb P(N(np) = k) - \mathbb P(B_{n,p} = k)} \le \frac C{\sqrt {np}}\pp{p\log^2n+\frac{\log^4n}{np}},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\sup_{|x|\le d_n}\max_{k\in J_{np}}\abs{\mathbb P(N((n+x)p) = k) - \mathbb P(N(np) = k)} \le \frac C{\sqrt {np}}\pp{\sqrt p\log^2n+\frac{\log^3n}{\sqrt{np}}},
\end{equation} 
for all $n\in{\mathbb N}, p\in[ n^{-\epsilon},1/2]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:gmc-full-support of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For every $x\in\Omega_{\rm tr}$,
\begin{equation}
        M_x(O)>0
        \qquad\text{for every non-empty open }O\subset D.
\end{equation}

