[Definition def: cocycle property of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] A random field $\Psi\colon \Omega \times \mathbb{Z}^{d} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfies the \emph{cocycle property} if for $\mathbb{P}$-a.e.\ $\omega$

  \begin{align}

    \Psi(\omega, y) - \Psi(\omega,x)
    \;=\;
    \Psi(\tau_{x}\omega, y-x),
    \qquad \forall\, x, y \in \mathbb{Z}^{d}.
  \end{align}

A random variable X has normal distribution \mathcal{N}(\mu, \sigma^2) with mean \mu \in \mathbb{R} and variance \sigma^2 \ge 0 if and only if its characteristic function is given by \phi_X(t) = \exp\left(i\mu t - \frac{1}{2} \sigma^2 t^2\right) for all t \in \mathbb{R}.
\mu \in \mathbb{R}
\sigma^2 \ge 0

[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2606.23383, 'Near-Lipschitz stability of the Kim--Milman flow map'] For any probability measure $\mu$ with $\mom(\mu) \defeq (\int \|x\|^2\,\mu(\!\dd x))^{1/2} < \infty$ and any $t > 0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \FI(q_t^\mu\mmid \gamma)
        &\le e^{-2t}\,\mom^2(\mu) + \frac{e^{-4t}}{1-e^{-2t}}\,d\,.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, if $\mom(\mu) \le \sqrt d$,
    \begin{align*}
        \FI(q_t^\mu\mmid \gamma)
        &\le \frac{de^{-2t}}{1-e^{-2t}}\,.
    \end{align*}

