body:
[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2608.06038, 'Efron type identities\\ for stopping sets and Poisson hulls'] Suppose that $Z$ is a Markov set and let
  $f\colon \BX\to\R_+$ be measurable with
  \begin{displaymath}
    \lambda(1-e^{-f})<\infty.
  \end{displaymath}
  Then
  \begin{align}
    \BE \big[\exp[-\eta_Z(f)+\lambda_Z(1-e^{-f})]\big]=1.
  \end{align}

