body:
[Lemma lemParameterAudit of arXiv:2609.00777, 'Universal murmuration and Hecke augmentation'] Assume all hypotheses of Theorem~(thm:scaled-murmuration of the paper), and put
\begin{equation*}
\eta=\frac{\delta_1}{2}-\delta_2.
\end{equation*}
Then the hyperbolic and parabolic errors used in the completion of Theorem~(thm:scaled-murmuration of the paper) are
$O(X^{-\eta+\varepsilon})$, apart from the displayed terms $X^\varepsilon\sqrt y/P$ and $(1+y)/P$.

