body:
[Lemma C(a) definition of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $f, \phi, u_\phi$ be as in Proposition (Bramson-psi-estimate-for-one-sided-f of the paper). Then, for $\alpha>0$ and $z= \alpha t+o(t)$,
\begin{equation}
C(f, \alpha) :=\lim_{t \to \infty} e^{\sqrt 2z} e^{\frac{z^2}{2t}}t^{\frac{1}{2}}u_{\phi}(t,z+\sqrt 2 t)
\end{equation}
exists, and is a strictly positive constant. The convergence in the right-hand side above is uniform for $\alpha$ in compact subsets of $(0,\infty)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def: nets of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $V_0 \subseteq V$. We say $V_0$ is \textbf{$a$-separated} if $d_G(x, y) \ge a$ for all $x, y \in V_0$. For $b\geq 1,$ we say that $V_{0}$ forms an \textbf{$(a, b)$-group net} of $G$ if the auxiliary graph $ G_{0}:= (V_{0},E_{0}),$ where
\begin{align*}
	E_0 := \big\{ \{x, y\}: x,y \in V_0, \, d_G(x, y) \le 4b \big\},
\end{align*}
satisfies that $p^{\mathrm{site}}_c(G_0) \le 3/4$.

[Dfn eq: restriction of a set to a closed ball of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] [{The local Hausdorff metric $\lHausdMet{S}{\rho_{S}}$}]
  For $A \in \mathcal{C}(S)$ and $r>0$,
  we write 
  \begin{equation}  
    A^{(r)} 
    \coloneqq 
    \closure(A \cap B_{d^{S}}(\rho, r)), 
  \end{equation}
  where we recall that $\closure(\cdot)$ denotes the closure of a set.
  We then define, for $A,B \in \mathcal{C}(S)$,
  \begin{equation}
    \lHausdMet{S}{\rho_{S}} (A, B) 
    \coloneqq 
    \int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-r} \bigl( 1 \wedge d_{H}^{S}(A^{(r)}, B^{(r)}) \bigr)\, dr.
  \end{equation}

[Lemma lem:support of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Assume that the force coefficient $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}_{\eps,\mu}^{\raisebox{0ex}{\includegraphics[scale=1.2]{figures/Xi.pdf}}}(t,s)$ is supported on the diagonal $\{t=s\}$. Then, for every $\tau\in\mathcal{T}$ and ${\eps,\mu}\in(0,1]$, we have the following support property of $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau}_{\eps,\mu}$:   
\begin{equs}    \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau_{\eps,\mu}(t,s^\tau)=0\;\text{$\mathrm{if}$}\; s^\tau\notin[t-2\mu{\mathfrak{o}}(\tau),t]^{\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}\,.
\end{equs}

[Definition eq:defTripleNorm of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] For every $N\geqslant1$, $\tau\in\mathcal{T}_*$ and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau} \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau]$, and  $\mu\in(0,1]$, set
    \begin{equs}        K^{\otimes 1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}_{N,\mu}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau(t,s^\tau)\eqdef \big(K_{N,\mu}\otimes\dots\otimes K_{N,\mu}\big)*\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau(t,s^\tau)\,.
    \end{equs}
We then endow $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau$ with the norm
    \begin{equs}       \nnorm{\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau}_{N,\mu} \eqdef \norm{K^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}_{N,\mu}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau}_{L^\infty_tL^1_{s^\tau}((-\infty,1]\times\R^{\mathfrak{s}(\tau)})}\equiv \sup_{t\leqslant1}\int_{\R^{\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}} |K^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}_{N,\mu} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau}(t,s^\tau)|\mathrm{d} s^\tau\,.\textcolor{white}{blabl}
    \end{equs}

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] Assume that conditions A1, A2, A3, A4 hold. Let $\mathbb{T}_n = \{t_1, \dots, t_n\}$, $\mathbb{T}_m = \{\tau_1, \dots, \tau_m\}$ be a micro and macro grids respectively, and $n = m^l$ for some $l > \frac{1}{\min(\gamma_2/2,\alpha_2,\beta)}$. Then, there exists a probability space supporting versions of the diffusion process $X_t$ and the Markov chain $Y_t$, and constants $C_1, C_2 > 0$ such that for every $1/2 < \alpha < 1$:
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{P} \left( \sup_{t \in [0,1]} |X_t - Y_t| \ge 2m^{\alpha-1} + 2K_1m^{-1} \right) \le C_1 m \Delta^{(n)} + 4md \exp\left(-\frac{m^{2\alpha-1}}{2C_2 d}\right),
\end{equation*}
where $K_1$ is the upper bound for the norm of the drift and $Y_t$ is the linear interpolation of the Markov chain. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 71 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $\ell \in \N$. 
Then there exist some constants $c,C>0$, depending only on $\ell$, such that for all $n\in \N$, we get that 
\begin{equation}
    \P_{\per}\left(C_{u,v}^{i,n,\ell} \, \forall (u;v)\in E_{\ell n} , i \in \lbr n\rbr \right) \geq 1-C\exp\big(-c n^{1/6} \big) . 
\end{equation}

