[Corollary cor:sig_vol_Fourier_laplace of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Let $\bm{\sigma} \in \TA[2]$ with $\deg(\bm{\sigma}) = N$ satisfy either the assumption  (equation eq:martingality_condition of the paper) {or $\rho = 0$ and $\bm{\sigma}^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}^{\otimes N}} \neq 0$}. Suppose that $u, v \in \mathbb{C}$ are such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \, \mathfrak{Re}(u) > 0, \quad \, \mathfrak{Re}\left(\dfrac{u^2(1-\rho^2) - u}{2} + v\right) < 0,
    \end{equation}
    and $\mathbb{E}\left[\exp({u\log(S_T / S_0) + v U_T})\,|\,\mathcal F_t\right] \neq 0$ a.s. for all $t \in [0\,,T]\,$.
    Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left({u\log\left({S_T}/{S_0}\right) + v U_T}\right)\,\big|\, \mathcal{F}_t\right] = \exp\left( \bracket{\bm{\psi}_t^{\sigW}}{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{\varnothing}}}}\right),
    \end{equation}
    where $\bm{\psi}^{\sigW[t]}$ is a solution to the Riccati equation (equation eq:Riccati_recentered of the paper) with $\sigX[] = \sigW[t]\,$,
    and $\bm{p}$ is given by
    \begin{equation}
        \bm{p} = u\rho\left(\bm{\sigma}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}} - \dfrac12\bm{\sigma}|_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{0}}}\right) + \left(\dfrac{u^2(1-\rho^2) - u}{2} + v \right)\bm{\sigma}^{\mathrel{\sqcup \mkern -3mu \sqcup} 2}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{0}}}.
    \end{equation}

[Lemma lem:2constant_local_holder of arXiv:2608.13452, 'Wasserstein stability of the zero cell of a Poisson hyperplane tessellation under directio'] Let \(\phi_0\) be a nondegenerate even probability measure on \(S^{d-1}\), let \(\gamma>0\) and let \(p \in [1,\infty)\).
    Then, there exist constants \(\varepsilon_0:=\varepsilon_0(\phi_0)\) and \(b_p(\phi_0)\), depending only on \(\phi_0\) and \(p\), such that, for every even probability measure \(\phi\) satisfying \(W_{\mathrm{geo}}(\phi,\phi_0)< \varepsilon_0\), we have 
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb{E}[R_0(Z_0(\phi))^p] \leq \frac{b_p(\phi_0)}{\gamma^p},
    \end{align}
    where \(Z_0(\phi)\) is the zero cell of the stationary Poisson hyperplane process with parameters \(\gamma\) and \(\phi\).

