[Lemma lem:disi of arXiv:2412.01381, 'Ergodicity and mixing for locally monotone stochastic evolution equations'] Assume hypotheses and notation of Theorem~(thm:main of the paper).
For any $x\in H$ and $0<s\leq t$
it follows that
\begin{equation}
\left(\mathcal{W}_2(P^*_t\delta_x,P^*_t\mu_\ast)\right)^2\leq \int_{H}
\int_{H}\left(\mathcal{W}_2(P^*_s\delta_z,P^*_s\delta_y)\right)^2 P^*_{t-s}\delta_x(\mathrm{d} z)\mu_\ast(\mathrm{d} y).
\end{equation}
In particular, it follows that
\begin{equation}
\left(\mathcal{W}_2(P^*_t\delta_x,\mu_\ast)\right)^2=\left(\mathcal{W}_2(P^*_t\delta_x,P^*_t\mu_\ast)\right)^2
\leq \int_{H} \left(\mathcal{W}_2(P^*_t\delta_x,P^*_t\delta_y)\right)^2\mu_\ast(\mathrm{d} y).
\end{equation}

