 \norm{  \varepsilon^{3+\kappa} (\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}_\varepsilon\tilde\Psi^\varepsilon)^3 (t)}_{\CC^{-3/2-\kappa}_\varepsilon}. 
\end{equation}
As above, we write $ X_\varepsilon = \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}_\varepsilon\tilde\Psi^\varepsilon$ for short as in (equation e:def-X of the ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:562a9a178bb3d0886a94da2a3ca54049cae23ae52a62a389f193776c11e33a94","revision_digest":"sha256:0a3d6abefee0cf9df70be4163711cabec61f7946593e041bcd027e8faa002dbc","source_id":"arxiv:2608.27828","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

body:
[Proposition 19 (a priori total-variation bound) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[proposition]{thm:ula-bias}
    Suppose $G'\in C^2_{\mathrm b}([0,\infty))$ and \cref{ass:moment,ass:contraction} hold.  For $\delta\in (1,2)$, there are $C,h_1>0$ such that, for all $h\in(0,h_1]$,
  \begin{equation}
    \|\pi_h-\pi\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\le C\,h^{\,\delta-1}.
  \end{equation}

[Proposition 24 (Prefix trace of a tree-reduced path) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $E$ be a finite-dimensional real vector space equipped with an auxiliary Euclidean norm, and let $\eta:[0,T]\to E$ satisfy the equivalent conditions of \cref{prop:reducedness}. Then
\begin{equation}
\set{S(\eta|_{[0,t]}):0\leq t\leq T}
 =[1,S(\eta)]
\end{equation}
in the Le Donne--Z\"ust signature tree. Every point of the endpoint geodesic is therefore attained by a prefix of the original parametrised path. The geodesic trace and its order are independent of the auxiliary Euclidean norm.

[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] Suppose that $1\le p_0< p_1 \le \infty$, $C,C_0\ge1$, and $g,h\in L^{p_0}\cap L^{p_1}(\ZZ^d)$ are non-negative. Assume that on any ball $B$, there exist $g_{B,0},g_{B,1}\ge0$  such that
    \begin{gather}
        g\le g_{B,0}+g_{B,1}, \quad g_{B,1}\le g+g_{B,0}\quad  \text{ on } B;\nonumber\\
        \Big(\fint_B|g_{B,0}|^{p_0}\Big)^{\frac1{p_0}} \le C\Big(\fint_{C_0B}|h|^{p_0}\Big)^{\frac1{p_0}};\\
        \Big(\fint_{\frac1{C_0}B}|g_{B,1}|^{p_1}\Big)^{\frac1{p_1}} \le C\Big(\fint_{B}|g_{B,1}|^{p_0}\Big)^{\frac1{p_0}}.
    \end{gather}
    Then for all $q\in(p_0,p_1)$,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{\ZZ^d} |g|^q\lesssim_{p_0,p_1,q,C,C_0}\int_{\ZZ^d} |h|^q. 
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Under~\eqref{h2},~\eqref{h3}, and~\eqref{h4}, there exists $\uc{c:fsc}>0$ such that, if
\begin{equation}
    \P_{\lambda} \big( \mathcal{C}(3n,n) \big) >1-\uc{c:fsc}, \text{ for some } n \in \N,
\end{equation}
then $\theta(\lambda) >0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def:scaledlabeledgraft of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix $\mu \in[0,1]$, $\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2\in\boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$, and $n\in N(\underline{\tau}_1)$. 
We define $$\graft_{n}^{\mu}: \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\underline{\tau}_1]  \otimes \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\underline{\tau}_2] \rightarrow \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_n \underline{\tau}_1]={\mcb{C}}[\underline{\tau}_1]\otimes{\mcb{C}}[\underline{\tau}_2+\ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2}]$$ as follows. For $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1} \in{\mcb{C}}[\underline{\tau}_1]$, $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2} \in{\mcb{C}}[\underline{\tau}_2]$ and using the shorthand ${\underline{\tau}}_{1,2,n} = \underline{\tau}_2 \graft_n \underline{\tau}_1$, we let 
\begin{equs}[eq:defB]
{}&
\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2} \graft_{n}^{\mu} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1}
\big)(t,s_{N({\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n}})})\equiv\graft_n^\mu\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1},\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2}\big)(t,s_{N({\underline{\tau}_{1,2,n}})})\\
{}& \enskip \eqdef  \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_1}(t,s_{N(\underline{\tau}_1)})\int_{0}^1 \dot G_\mu(s_n-w )(\boldsymbol{\ell}_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\underline{\tau}_2})(w,s_{N({\underline{\tau}_2}+\ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2})}) \mathrm{d} w\,
    \in \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\underline{\tau}] \,.\textcolor{white}{blabla}
\end{equs}

[Lem 25 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>4$. There exists $C_1>0$ such that the following holds. For every $\beta<\beta_c$, and every $n\geq C_1(\beta_c-\beta)^{-1/2}$, there exists $S\subset \Lambda_{n/2}$ containing $0$ such that
\begin{equation}
	\varphi_{\beta}(S)\leq \frac{1}{10}.
\end{equation}

