[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2606.03661, '2606.03661'] The solution to equation \eqref{mathcal.eq.1}, with initial condition $f(0)=1$, is given by
\begin{equation}

f(t) = \Psi_\alpha^\nu(-\kappa t)  := 
\frac{G(1+\nu)}{G(2-\alpha+\nu)}\sum_{n=0}^\infty   \frac{G(2+n-\alpha+\nu)}{G(1+n+\nu)} \frac{(-\kappa t)^n}{n!} ,
\end{equation}
where $G(\cdot)$ is the Barnes $G$-function (see Appendix~\ref{appendix.Barnes}).

