[Lemma lem:correlation_stopping of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There is some $\lambda_0 > 1$ and $C, c > 0$ such that for all $\lambda \geqslant \lambda_0$
and all $k \in \mathbb{N}$, when $\mathbf{X}$ and $\mathbf{Y}$ are sampled independently we have
\begin{equation}
    \tau_\ell^{0,k} < 0 < \tau_r^{0,k}
    \qquad \text{and} \qquad
    \tau_\ell^{t,k} < t < \tau_r^{t,k}
\end{equation}
with probability at least $1 - C e^{-ct}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] We have the cointeraction property 
	\begin{align*}
		(\Delta_r^- \otimes \operatorname{id})\Delta^\partial = (\operatorname{id} \otimes \Delta^\partial) \Delta_r^-.
	\end{align*}
	for the operations on $\mcT$.

