[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.23383, 'Near-Lipschitz stability of the Kim--Milman flow map'] For $\mu \in \cP_2(\mathbb{R}^d)$ which satisfies \eqref{theta}, and any $\nu \in \cP_2(\mathbb{R}^d)$, it holds that
\begin{align}
\|\mathsf T^{\mu} - \mathsf T^{\nu}\|_{L^2(\gamma)}^2 \leq 2L_0^2(\mu) \, {\mathsf H}(\nu\mmid\mu)\,,
\end{align}
where $$L_0(\mu) \deq \exp\Bigl(\int_0^\infty \theta_t \dd t\Bigr)\, .$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Let $ f $ be a random variable. If $ f $ is Bochner integrable with respect to the probability measure $ \mathbb{P} $, then we denote 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{E} f = \int_{\Omega} f d \mathbb{P}
    \end{align*}
    and call it the mean or mathematical expectation of $ f $.

