{"artifact_digest":"sha256:aaad32c1034209381c21aa61113c921101fe58bd468c249a8dd1f0ce4840030f","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/aa/aaad32c1034209381c21aa61113c921101fe58bd468c249a8dd1f0ce4840030f.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:0497c289f50e708a41bb21518fec15133c080043e7fda6dd0bc20628b1226d36","bundle_entry_key":"2605-30030-theorem-11-m-formula","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_040","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_040.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-30030-theorem-11-m-formula","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Fix~$F$ as in the statement. 
The Baxter--Kelland--Wu correspondence (see \cite{baxter1976equivalence,DumManTas16b,magicformula}) implies that 
\begin{align*}
    \rcP_{\delta}[\mathcal A_F(\calL)]=\mathbb E^{\rm 6V}_{\delta}\Big[\exp\Big(i\int_{\R^2} F(z)h(z)\d z\Big)\Big],
