body:
[Conj GW:vertex of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] For $n\in\{1,\ldots,5\}$ and curve class $\beta = [C_1]+\cdots+[C_n]$, the equivariant Gromov--Witten theory of $Z_n$ is given by
    \begin{equation}

       \GWargs{Z_n}{\mathsf{T}}{\beta} 
       =
       \hat{\mathsf{A}}_{\mathsf{T}}\bigl( \overline{M}_{0}(Z_n,\beta) \bigr) \,,
    \end{equation}
    where $\overline{M}_{0}(Z_n,\beta)$ denotes the moduli space of genus-zero stable maps to $Z_n$ in curve class $\beta$. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Proposition sumeq of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] For any $k\leq m <  n$ and $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$, we have
\begin{align} 
\sum_{i=k}^n\big[h^i(x) - h^i(y)\big] 
= \sum_{i=k}^n \big[(\sigma^m h)^i(x) -  (\sigma^m h)^i(y)\big] 
= \sum_{i=k}^n \big[(\sigma_{m} h)^i(x) -  (\sigma_{m} h)^i(y)\big].
\end{align}

