[Lemma of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Suppose we are in the set-up of Theorem (thm:convbls of the paper) with $a > 0$. Consider the boundary cluster that is given by the closed union of all critical Brownian loop soup clusters that intersect at least one boundary to boundary excursion, denote it by $\widetilde C_{a}^{m}$ for the metric graph, and by $C_{a}$ for the continuum.

Then for any $z_1, \dots, z_n \in D$, and any 
$\varepsilon_1, \dots, \varepsilon_n > 0$, 
we have that the probabilities
$$\tilde p^{\rm bd}_{a,m} := \mathbb{P}\left(\nexists \widetilde \gamma \in \widetilde C_{a}^m\text{ such that} \sum_{j=1}^{n}
\indx_{\widetilde \gamma}(z_j)
\text{ odd}
 \: \& \: \widetilde C_{a}^{m} \cap \bigcup_{j=1}^n\mathbb{D}(z_j, \varepsilon_j) = \emptyset\right),$$  

converge, as $m \to \infty$, to 
$$p^{\rm bd}_a := \mathbb{P}\left(\nexists \gamma \in C_{a}\text{ such that} \sum_{j=1}^{n}
\indx_{\gamma}(z_j)
\text{ odd}
 \: \& \: C_{a} \cap \bigcup_{j=1}^n\mathbb{D}(z_j, \varepsilon_j) = \emptyset\right).$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 55 of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every $s\ge1$ and $k\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\{s+i\}\in(q;q)_k\Z[q^{\pm1}].
\end{equation}

[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2606.31133, 'Level-dependent quasi-birth-and-death processes: Application to cost analysis of multi-ser'] We have,
\begin{eqnarray}
\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{n,n+k}(s)&=&
\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{n,n+1}(s)
\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{n+1,n+2}(s)
\times
\cdots
\times
\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{n+k-1,n+k}(s),
\end{eqnarray}
where
\begin{eqnarray}
\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{0,1}(s)&=&
-({\bf Q}^{[0,0]}-s{\bf C}_0\times I(0\in\mathcal{A}))^{-1}
{\bf Q}^{[0,1]},
\end{eqnarray} 
and for $n=1,\ldots,n+k-1$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{n,n+1}(s)&=&
-({\bf Q}^{[n,n]}-s{\bf C}_n\times I(n\in\mathcal{A})
+{\bf Q}^{[n,n-1]}\widetilde{\bf C}_{\mathcal{A}}^{n-1,n}(s)
)^{-1}
{\bf Q}^{[n,n+1]}.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 9 (Search--validation phase law) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] If $m,N\to\infty$ with $m^2/N\to\tau\in(0,\infty)$, then
\begin{equation}
B_{m,N}\longrightarrow
B(\tau):=\vartheta_4\!\left(0,e^{-\pi^2/(4\tau)}\right).

\end{equation}
Define $\tau_\varepsilon=\inf\{\tau>0:B(\tau)\le\varepsilon\}$. After first taking the joint limit at fixed $\tau$ and then letting $\varepsilon\downarrow0$,
\begin{equation}
\tau_\varepsilon=\log\frac1\varepsilon
+\frac12\log\log\frac1\varepsilon
+\log\frac4{\sqrt\pi}+o(1).

\end{equation}
No uniform finite-$(m,N)$ statement is asserted for an arbitrary sequence $\varepsilon=\varepsilon_N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 6 (Cap interpolation) of arXiv:2607.23980, 'Sharp small-deviation inequalities for sums of independent\\nonnegative random variables'] Let $C\subset\R^m$ be a convex body with centroid $g_C$. Suppose that $L$ is affine and nonnegative on $C$, and put $a=L(g_C)>0$. Then, for $0\le t\le a$,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\vol_m(C\cap\{L\ge t\})}{\vol_m(C)}
 \ge\left(1-\frac{t}{(m+1)a}\right)^m.
\end{equation}
The estimate is sharp.

