body:
[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2603.28093, 'Random Stability of Random Variables'] Pick a distribution $Q$ on the half-line. Assume $G(Q)$ is nontrivial. Then the random variable $N_c$ with probability generating function~\eqref{eq:Bunge} with $L$ being the Laplace transform of $Y$ satisfies 
\begin{equation}

\frac{N_c}{c} \stackrel{d}{\to} Y,\quad c \to \infty,\quad c \in S(Q), 
\end{equation}
if and only if $\mathbb E[N_c\ln N_c] < \infty$. In this case, $\mathbb E[Y] = 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

