[Cor cor14 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Let $p\ge 2$. Then there exist $\Gamma_4=\Gamma_4(p,a,h)>0$ and $\Gamma_5=\Gamma_5(p,a,h)>0$ such that if ((init of the paper)) 
  and ((uut of the paper)) hold with $\delta_1=\delta_1(h)$ as in Lemma (lem11 of the paper) and with some $T\in (0,T_{max}]$, then the function ${\mathcal{F}}_1$
  from ((F1 of the paper)) satisfies
  \begin{eqnarray}\label{14.1}
	& & \hspace*{-20mm}
	\frac{d}{dt} {\mathcal{F}}_1^\frac{p}{2}(t)
	+ \Gamma_4 \cdot {\mathcal{F}}_1^\frac{p}{2}(t)

	\nonumber\\
	&\le& \Gamma_5 \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |u| \cdot |f(u,u_t,\nabla u, \nabla u_t)| \bigg\}^\frac{p}{2}
	+ \Gamma_5 \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |v|\cdot |f(u,u_t,\nabla u,\nabla u_t)|\bigg\}^\frac{p}{2} \nonumber\\
	& & + \Gamma_5 \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |u|^3 \bigg\}^\frac{p}{2}
	+ \Gamma_5 \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |v|^3 \bigg\}^\frac{p}{2}
	\qquad \mbox{for all } t\in (0,T).
  \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

