[Lemma lem: dimension bound of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $\lambda\vdash n$, and $r:=n-\lambda_1$. Then, we have
\begin{enumerate}
\item $d_\lambda\le\binom{n}{r}\cdot d_{\lambda^*}\le\binom{n}{r}\cdot \sqrt{r!}\le n^r/\sqrt{r!}.$
\item When $r\le \log n$, we have 
$$d_\lambda=\binom{n}{r}\cdot d_{\lambda^*}\left(1-\frac{r}{n}+O(n^{-2+o(1)})\right).$$
\end{enumerate}

