body:
[Prop late-catch-up of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that Equation~(equation eq:persistent of the paper) is satisfied for $\alpha > 0$ and $K \in \mathbb{N}$. Then, for any $u \in \mathcal{U}$,  
    \begin{equation}
       \E{\left| \left\{v = v_1 \cdots v_{m} \in \mathcal{U} \colon v_1 \geq K, uv\text{ catches up to } u \right\}\right| }= \sum_{v\in \mathcal{U}\colon v_1 \geq K} \Prob{uv \text{ catches up to } u} < \infty. 
    \end{equation}

