body:
[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] For $0\le p<(4a-1)/4a$, we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to \infty}\frac{\langle M\rangle_n}{n^{4a(1-p)-1}}=\frac{(\Gamma(a(2p-1)+1))^2}{4a(1-p)-1}\ \ \text{a.s.}
\end{equation}
and for $p=(4a-1)/4a$, we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to \infty}\frac{\langle M\rangle_n}{\log n}=\Big(\Gamma\Big(a+\frac{1}{2}\Big)\Big)^2\ \ \text{a.s.}
\end{equation}

