[Lemma 67 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the same notation as in Definition \ref{Def.LETop}. For any $s \in [0, \bar{\kappa})$, we can find $\epsilon > 0$, depending on $q,c,s$, such that 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N \rightarrow \infty} \mathbb{P}_N \left( L_2^N(\lfloor tN\rfloor ) \geq h_2(t)N - \epsilon N \mbox{ for some }t \in [0, s] \right) = 0.
\end{equation}

