body:
[Definition of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] From a set $D = \mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B) \subset \mathscr{B}_{k-1}$ having $|\mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B)|\le s_k$, we construct $R_1,...,R_K$ as follows. Start with candidate set $\mathcal R = \{B': B'\in \mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B)\}$;  repeat the following process
        \begin{itemize}
            \item If the current candidate $\mathcal R$ contains two squares $R, R'$ of side-length $a \ell_{k-1}$ and $b \ell_{k-1}$ within distance $10 \ell_{k-1}$, then replace $R,R'$ in $\mathcal R$ with $R''$ which is a smallest square covering both squares.  
        \end{itemize}

