[Theorem lem:full_supp_meas_full_supp_cop of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] Let $C \in \mathcal{C}_{ar}^d$ and let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}_d}$ be its corresponding Williamson measure. Then the following assertions hold
    \begin{itemize}
     \item[(i)] If $\gamma^{abs}$ has full support, then $\mu_C^{abs}$ has full support.
        \item[(ii)] If $\gamma^{dis}$ has full support, then $\mu_C^{dis}$ has full support.
         \item[(iii)] If $\gamma^{sing}$ has full support, then $\mu_C^{sing}$ has full support.
    \end{itemize}

[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] For every $\mathcal{I}=[t_1,t_2]\subset[0,\infty)$ and $\mathcal{J}=[\underline{a},\overline{a}]\subset(0,1)$ it holds that
    \begin{equation*}
        V_T\to V_\infty
    \end{equation*}
    uniformly on $\mathcal{I}\times\mathcal{J}$ for $T\to\infty$.

