[Theorem thm: main result of arXiv:2411.05924, 'Non-negative Martingale Solutions to the Stochastic Porous Medium Equation with Sticky Beh'] There exists a stochastic basis $(\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb F, \mathbb P)$ supporting processes $u \in \bigcap_{\delta\in(0,1)} \Xi^\delta_{\mathfrak u}$, $u_n \in C([0,T], L^2)$ for $n\in\mathbb N$ and $Q$--Wiener processes $W$ and $W_n$ for $n\in\mathbb N$, s.t.~$((\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb F, \mathbb P), u, W)$ is a non-negative martingale solution to the stochastic porous medium equation (equation eq: intro1 of the paper)--(equation eq: intro3 of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def: solution of the paper), satisfying for any $p \geq 1$
    \begin{equation}

        \mathbb E\left[\sup_{r\in[0,T]} \left\| u(r) \right\|_{H^{(\alpha-2)/\alpha}_0}^p \right] + \mathbb E\left[\int_0^T \left\| u(r) \right\|_{H^1_0}^p \mathrm d r \right] < \infty.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, for any $n\in\mathbb N$ the triples $\left((\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb F, \mathbb P), P_n(u_n), W_n \right)$ are martingale solutions to (equation eq: discrete dynamics Rn of the paper) in the sense of Proposition (prop: existence for discrete systems of the paper), and there exists a subsequence of $u_n$ converging to $u$ $\mathbb P$-a.s.~in $\Xi_u$. Furthermore, if for some $\varepsilon > 0$ the pre-limiting systems satisfy
    \begin{equation}

        \limsup_{n\rightarrow\infty} \mathbb P (\mathcal S(u_n) \geq \varepsilon) > 0,
    \end{equation}
    then the system (equation eq: intro1 of the paper)--(equation eq: intro3 of the paper) exhibits sticky behavior (equation eq: limiting stickiness condition of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Assume~\eqref{h2},~\eqref{h3}, and $\theta(\lambda)>0$. Then
    \begin{equation}
        \inf_{n \geq 0} \P_{\lambda}\big( \mathcal{C}(n,n) \big) >0.
    \end{equation}

