[Prop 6 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] Take any $A_\alpha = \alpha P + (1-\alpha)G$ with $G$ as the Gibbs kernel, and $P$ a $\pi$-reversible kernel. Then for any positive integer $l \geq 2$ and $\alpha \in (0,1)$,
    \begin{equation}
        \| A_\alpha^l - \Pi\|_{F,\pi}^2 \leq (1-\alpha \gamma^*(P))^{2(l-1)} \| A_\alpha - \Pi\|_{F,\pi}^2
    \end{equation}

