[Lem l:1103.17 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] There exists $C < \infty$ such that for all $n \geq 1$,
\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{V}{\rm ar} \bigg( \sum_{x \in {\rm D}_n} h^2_n(x)\bigg)  \leq C |{\rm D}_n|^2 \,.
\end{equation}

