[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2606.29512, '2606.29512'] Let $u$ be an $\R^d$-valued admissible function and let
$v,w\in C^{\infty}_0(\cR,\bR^d)$. 
Then for $\P\otimes dt$-almost every $(\omega,t)$ we have 
\begin{align}
|b(u_t,v,w)|&\leq N\hat u \big(|Dw|_{L_2}|w|_{L_2}\big)|Dv|_{L_2}  
                                                                                  \nonumber\\
&\quad+\bar u_t|Dv|_{L_2}|w|_{L_2}                         \nonumber
\end{align}
with a constant $N=N(d,r)$.

[Proposition of arXiv:2604.23981, 'Accelerating sampling via asymptotic relaxation enhancing flows'] Suppose $v$ is relaxation enhancing in $\mathcal{Y}\subset L^2(\pi)$. Suppose that $q_0$ satisfies Assumption (ass:warmstart of the paper) with $q_0-1\in \mathcal{Y}$. Then, for any given $B>0$ and $t>0$, there is $A_0$, whenever $A>A_0$, one has
\begin{equation}
H(t)\le H_0\exp(-B t),
\end{equation}
where $H(t)$ is defined as (equation eq:Ht of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

