body:
[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2512.05340, 'The rate of convergence of the critical mean-field $O(N)$ magnetization via multivariate n'] Let $u: \RR \to \RR^{d}$ be such that $|u(t)|^{2} \in C^{1}(\RR, \RR)$. Suppose it satisfies the following differential inequality
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\diff}{\dt}|u(t)|^{2} \leq 2a(t)|u(t)|^{2} + 2b(t)|u(t)|, \qquad \forall t \in (0, T),
    \end{equation}
    where $T \in (0, \infty)$, $a, b \in L^{1}([0, T])$ and $b \geq 0$. If $|u(0)| = 0$ then
    \begin{equation}
        |u(t)| \leq \int_{0}^{t}b(s)\exp\left(\int_{s}^{t}a(r)\, \dr\right)\, \ds, \qquad \forall t \in [0, T).
    \end{equation}

