[Cor Zn-small-four of arXiv:2608.23135, 'Graph distance and effective resistance of the random walk trace in four and five dimensio'] Fix $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$. 
There exists $C<\infty$, independent of $\varepsilon$, such that for all $n$,
\begin{equation}

        \mathbb E\bigl[(Z_n^{\varepsilon})^2\bigr]\le C\varepsilon.
\end{equation}

[Defn genfineslopetop of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] For $s\in \mathbb{R}$, we declare the following set to be open in $\widehat{\mathscr{S}}$:
    \begin{align}
        &\big\{t^\heartsuit \mid t\in (s, +\infty]\big\} \cup \big\{s^\sharp, s^\dagger\big\},\\
        &\big\{t^\heartsuit \mid t\in [-\infty, s)\big\} \cup \big\{s^\flat, s^\dagger\big\}
    \end{align}
    The following two sets are also open:
    \begin{align}
        &\big\{+\!\infty^\sharp, \aleph^\sharp, \aleph^\dagger\big\},\\
        &\big\{-\!\infty^\flat, \aleph^\flat, \aleph^\dagger\big\}
    \end{align}
    We define the topology on $\mathscr{S}$ to be the topology generated by these open sets.

[Theorem 52 (Triangular canonical extraction) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Run the stages in the lexicographic order
\begin{equation}
 n\to\mathcal U,\qquad
 J_1\to\infty,\quad J_2\to\infty,\quad\ldots,\quad J_Q\to\infty,

\end{equation}
finishing weight $s$ before starting $s+1$.  Then at every finite internal extraction
level
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb U_s^{-1}M_s^{[J]}\subset\mathscr A_s,

\end{equation}
and at the end of stage $s$
\begin{equation}
 A_{a,s}=y_{a,s},\qquad r_{a,s}=g_{a,s}.

\end{equation}
Quantitatively,
\begin{equation}
 0\le\widehat N_s\le QR^2\Id,\qquad
 \lambda_{\max}(\widehat E_s)\ge\frac{\widehat{\mathfrak H}_s}{d},

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \sum_a\norm{P_{V_s^\triangle}r_{a,s}}^2
 \ge
 \frac{\widehat{\mathfrak H}_s}{dQR^2}.

\end{equation}
Thus the scale-invariant per-weight capture constant is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\kappa_{Q,d}^\triangle=\frac1{dQ}}.

\end{equation}
With threshold
\begin{equation}
 \delta_{s,J}=\frac{dQR^4}{J},

\end{equation}
fewer than $J$ promotions occur at weight $s$, and
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{j\ge0}\widehat{\mathfrak H}_s^{[j]}\le dQR^4,
 \qquad
 \widehat{\mathfrak H}_s\longrightarrow0.

\end{equation}
After all weights,
\begin{equation}
 A=A^{\can},\qquad
 r=G^{\can},\qquad
 G^{\can}\indep A^{\can}.

\end{equation}

