[Theorem eq:LT1-Palm of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Consider the motion model with speed $v=1$. Under the Palm probability measure $\mathbb{P}^0_{\mathcal V }$, the Laplace transform of the inter-handover time $T$ is given by,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}^0_{\mathcal V }\left[e^{-\rho T}\right] = 2\pi \lambda^{\frac 5 2}
\int_{(\mathbb{R}^+)^5} e^{-\rho (\hat s_1-\hat s)}
 e^{-2\lambda \vert U^{\hat s_1}_{\hat h_1}\cup U^{\hat s}_{\hat h}\vert}
 {\rm d}t_3\, {\rm d} h_3\, {\rm d} t_2\, {\rm d} h_2\, {\rm d} h_1, 

\end{equation}
    for any $\rho\geq 0$, where $\hat s=\frac{h_1^2-t_2^2-h_2^2}{2t_2}, \hat h^2=\frac{1}{4}\left[t_2^2+2(h_1^2+h_2^2)+\frac{(h_2^2-h_1^2)^2}{t_2^2}\right]$, 
    $\hat s_1=\frac{t_3^2+h_3^2-h_1^2}{2t_3}$ and $\hat h_1^2=\frac{1}{4}\left[t_3^2+2(h_1^2+h_3^2)+\frac{(h_3^2-h_1^2)^2}{t_3^2}\right]$ and $\vert U^{\hat s}_{\hat h}\cup U^{\hat s_1}_{\hat h_1}\vert $ is evaluated in Lemma~(lemma:UcupU of the paper).

