[Proposition 44 (Balanced reduction) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Assume that $\xi$ is balanced with respect to $\lambda$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{d.balanced_comparison_structure}. Let $f$ be the limit free energy, or equivalently the Hopf formula in Theorem~\ref{t.main}. Then, for every $t\geq0$ and every $q\in\mcl Q_2^\sS$,
\begin{equation}

    u(t,q^\lambda)\leq f(t,q)\leq \sum_{s\in\sS}\lambda_s u(t,q_s).
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}

    f(t,0)=u(t,0),\qquad t\geq0.
\end{equation}

