[Prop 10 of arXiv:2608.26642, '2608.26642'] Assume that $I-T^\mu$ is invertible; equivalently, $1$ does not belong to the spectrum of $T^\mu$. Then the unique solution to equation (\ref{limit-eq}) is
\begin{align}
  f=\frac{(I-T^\mu)^{-1}1}{\mu[(I-T^\mu)^{-1}1]},\qquad C=\frac{1}{\mu[(I-T^\mu)^{-1}1]}.
\end{align}

