[Lemma 12 (A harmonic Robin Liouville lemma) of arXiv:2608.30211, '2608.30211'] Let $v\in C^2(\Hh^d)\cap C^1(\overline{\Hh^d})$ be bounded and harmonic.
If
\begin{equation}
 \partial_\nu v+v=0\quad\text{on }\partial\Hh^d,
\end{equation}
then $v\equiv0$.

[Definition 2 of arXiv:2609.02699, '\vspace{-0.5 cm}Gauge theory and symplectic structures'] For $m\in\mathbb N, m>1$, we define a constant $c_m$ by the following equation
\begin{align*}
    \frac{1}{2^{m-1}}\int_M q(\psi_0)\wedge \omega^{m-1}=ic_m\int_M \omega^m
\end{align*}

