[Lem 6 of arXiv:2609.01101, '2609.01101'] Assume GRH for $\zeta_L$.  For every intermediate field $K$ of $L/\Q$,
the function
\begin{equation}
\Phi_K(z)=\frac{z-1}{z+1}\zeta_K(z)
\end{equation}
is analytic and zero-free in $\Re z>1/2$.

[Lemma lem:capacitydecomp of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let $A=\{x_1,\ldots,x_n\}\subset\mathbb{Z}^d$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \Ca(A)=\sum_{k=1}^n\mathbb{P}_{x_k}(W[1,\infty)\cap\{x_1,\ldots,x_k\}=\varnothing)\mathbb{P}_{x_k}(W[1,\infty)\cap\{x_1,\ldots,x_{k-1}\}=\varnothing).
\end{equation}

