body:
[Lem of arXiv:2608.06500, 'Free energy of Ising models under a spectral condition'] For any $\varepsilon,t,\delta>0$, and an $\alpha$-good potential $V$,
     there exists a local function
    $q_{\varepsilon}:\mathcal{G}_{[0,C],C}\times[0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^N$ which can be written
    as a finite sum

    \begin{align*}
    \text{\boldmath $q$}_{\varepsilon}(G;\beta) = \sum_{X\in\mathcal{S}} c_X(\beta) \text{\boldmath $t$}(X,G)\, ,
    \end{align*}
    such that $\mathcal{S}$ is a finite set, the coefficients $c_X(\beta)$
    are  polynomials in $\beta$ independent of $G$, and 
    for all $G\in\mathcal{G}_{[0,C],C}$ and $\beta\in[0,1]$, we have (for $K=t/\delta$)

    \begin{align*}
    \left| \frac{1}{N}\mathbb{E}[H(\text{\boldmath $\psi$}^{(K)})] - q_{\varepsilon} (G;\beta) \right| \le \varepsilon.
    \end{align*}

