[Prop 14 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $H \in \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R})$, $s \in [0,T]$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$. Then
\begin{align}
	& \Theta(n) \big\{  \mcb L^n[\mathcal{Z}_{s}^n(H)]^{2} -2 \mathcal{Z}_{s}^n(H) \mcb L^n \mathcal{Z}_{s}^n(H)  \big\} \nonumber \\
	= &\frac{\Theta(n)}{2n} \sum_{ z, w } \big[ H ( \tfrac{z - s v_n  }{n}  ) - H ( \tfrac{w - s v_n  }{n}  ) \big]^{2} [f_w( \eta_s^n ) - f_z( \eta_s^n )]^{2} [ p(w-z) r^n_{z,w}(\eta_s^n) + p(z-w) r^n_{w,z}(\eta_s^n) ]. 
\end{align}

[Lem lem_maximum_hitting_time_of_0 of arXiv:2411.13964, 'Long-time analysis of a pair of on-lattice and continuous run-and-tumble particles with ja'] Let $\tau = \inf \left\{ t \ge 0 : X_D(t) = (0, *^0_{(1, -1)} ) \right\}$. There exists $C > 0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\sup_{X_0 \in E_D} E_{X_0} \left[\tau\right] \le C \frac{1}{\omega} \left(1 + \omega^2 \ell^2\right).
\end{align*}

