[Lem 33 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] There exist constants $\varepsilon > 0$ and $C>1$ such that the following holds for any $q,q' \in [-\varepsilon, \varepsilon]$, with $q \ge q'$, and $z \in \mathfrak{X}$. For each $\mathfrak{e}_z \in \{ \mathfrak{e}_{z;q}, \mathfrak{e}_{z;q'} \}$, we have 
                       \begin{multline}

            \mathcal{H}_{q'} (z) + C^{-1} (\mathfrak{d}_z \mathfrak{e}_z)^{1/2} (q-q') - C \mathfrak{d}_z^{1/2} (q-q')^{3/2} \\ 
            \le \mathcal{H}_q (z) \le \mathcal{H}_{q'} (z) + C(\mathfrak{d}_z \mathfrak{e}_{z})^{1/2} (q-q') + C \mathfrak{d}_z^{1/2} (q-q')^{3/2}.                        
\end{multline}

\noindent In addition, we have 
    \begin{flalign}

             \mathcal{H}_q (z) \ge \mathcal{H}_{q'} (z) + C^{-1} (\mathfrak{d}_z \mathfrak{e}_z)^{1/2} (q-q').                       
\end{flalign} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 11 (Consistency of empirical endpoint calibration) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:rcm-calibration},
\begin{equation}
\varepsilon_{{\rm end},N}
\leq\varepsilon_{{\rm end,app},N}
+2\delta_{{\rm end},N}
+\varepsilon_{{\rm end,opt},N},
\end{equation}
and hence \(\varepsilon_{{\rm end},N}\to0\) in probability. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

