{"artifact_digest":"sha256:a9bdb2f9e29f934cfb089ed978565395d13c7792def5d127a139c617ae19ea7b","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/a9/a9bdb2f9e29f934cfb089ed978565395d13c7792def5d127a139c617ae19ea7b.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:bdd6a2bac597ea5e0b028b12e9608fc8044e9625c314bee8f5b3784067b29f92","bundle_entry_key":"2608-12291-theorem-14-fbp-homogeneous","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_094","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_094.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-12291-theorem-14-fbp-homogeneous","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We rewrite the ODE in \eqref{ode} as 
    \begin{equation}
        \widehat V''(x)=-\frac{2c}{\sigma^2(x)}.
    \end{equation}
    Let $\psi$ be any particular solution to the inhomogeneous ODE \eqref{ode2}. Then the general solution is $\psi(x)+c_1 x+c_2$ for constants $c_1$ and $c_2$. Using the boundary conditions for smooth and continuous fit, \eqref{cont} and \eqref{smooth}, at $A$, we get the representation for the candidate solution
    \begin{equation}
        \widehat V_A(x) := (x-A)(g'(A)-\psi'(A))+g(A)-\psi(A)+\psi(x)
    \end{equation}
    for $x\in(A,B)$.

