[Definition def:dsm of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] Let $\{g_{\theta}\}_{\theta\in\Theta}$ be a family of maps sending a self-adjoint
operator to a self-adjoint operator, and let $w:[0,T]\to(0,\infty)$ be a weight.
Define
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal L(\theta)=\int_{0}^{T}w(t)\;
  \tau\Big[\big(g_{\theta}(X_{t},t)-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,X_{0}\big)^{2}\Big]\mathrm{d} t,
\end{equation}
and, given a minimiser $\theta^{\star}$, the estimated free score
\begin{equation}
  \widehat\xi_{t}(X_{t})=\frac{1}{v_{t}}\big(X_{t}-g_{\theta^{\star}}(X_{t},t)\big).
\end{equation}

