[Lemma S33L of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] Fix $p, M, \epsilon, \eta \in (0, \infty)$, and $\sigma = \sqrt{p(1+p)}$. There exist $N_3 \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\delta$, depending on $p, M, \epsilon, \eta$, such that the following holds. If $n \geq N_3$, $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$ are such that $x \leq y$ and $|x| \leq M n^{1/2}$, $|y - pn| \leq M n^{1/2}$, and $\mathcal{Q}_1\in C([0,1])$ is defined by $\mathcal{Q}_1(t) = \sigma^{-1}n^{-1/2}(Q_1(tn) - ptn)$, then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}_{\operatorname{Geom}}^{0,n, x, y} \left( w(\mathcal{Q}_1, \delta) > \epsilon \right) < \eta.
\end{equation}

