[Definition eq:ME_density of arXiv:2604.08889, 'Matrix Representations for Scale Functions of Spectrally Negative Lévy Processes with Rati'] A distribution on $(0,\infty)$ is called \emph{matrix-exponential} (ME) if its density can be written as
\begin{equation}
f(x) = \bm{\alpha} \mathrm{e}^{\bm{T}x} \bm{t}, \qquad x > 0,
\end{equation}
where $\bm{\alpha}$ is a $1 \times p$ row vector, $\bm{T}$ is an $p \times p$ matrix, $\bm{t}$ is an $p \times 1$ column vector, and $p\in \mathbb{N}$. 
The triplet $(\bm{\alpha}, \bm{T}, \bm{t})$ is called a \emph{matrix-exponential representation} of order $p$.

[Lemma 36 (Fourier--Duhamel trace derivative bound) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] Let \(h\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R)\), let \(A=A^{\mathsf T}\), and let
\(B=B^{\mathsf T}\).  For every integer \(r\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{u\in\mathbb R}
 \left|\frac{\dd^r}{\dd u^r}\Tr h(A+uB)\right|
 \le
 C_{h,r}\norm{B}_1\norm{B}_{\op}^{r-1},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
 C_{h,r}:=\frac1{2\pi}\int_{\mathbb R}
 |t|^r|\widehat h(t)|\,\dd t<\infty.
\end{equation}
The constant is independent of the dimension and of \(A\).

[Lemma exponential_bound_Nt of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $S \subset V$ be a finite set containing the origin. For $x \in S$ define $D_x := d_{\vec{G}}(x, S^c).$ We have that for any $t > 0$ and $x\in S:$
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E_x\left[ N(t) \, \big\vert \, \tau_{S^c} \le t \right] \leq \Delta^{D_x} (t + D_x) \, .
\end{equation}

