[Lemma L:M-lemma of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] For $\mathcal{M}^\rho$ from Definition (D:prelandscapes of the paper), it has a continuous extension to $\mathbb H^2_\uparrow$, and this extension satisfies parts $1, 2, 4, 5, 6$, and $7$ of Proposition (P:properties-elpp of the paper) (in the place of $\mathcal{Q}^\rho$ there).    
        Moreover, for any $q > 0, c \in \mathbb{R}$ if we consider the rescaling
        \begin{equation}

            \mathcal{M}^{\rho, q, c}(x, s; y, t) := q^{-1} \mathcal{M}^\rho(q^2 x, q^3 s + c; q^2 y, q^3 t + c)
        \end{equation}
        then $\mathcal{M}^{\rho, q, c}|_{\mathbb{Q}^4 \cap \mathbb H^2_\uparrow}$ is a half-space pre-landscape of parameter $q \alpha$.

[Prop 39 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $p=p(\xi)$ be of the form
    \begin{equation*}
        p(\xi)=\sum_{k\in \Lambda}p_ke^{2i\pi \ps{k}{\xi}}, \quad\xi\in \T^d,
    \end{equation*}
    where $\Lambda=\prod_{j=1}^d\disc{-n_j}{m_j}$, $n_j,m_j\geq 0$ and $p_k\in \C$, $k\in \Lambda$. We assume that 
    \begin{equation}
        \exists \hspace{0.1cm }k\in \Lambda\setminus \{0\}, \m p_k\neq 0.
    \end{equation}
    Let us denote 
    \begin{equation*}
        S:=\sum_{j=1}^d (n_j+m_j)>0, \mm \Xi:=\prod_{j=1}^d(n_j+m_j+1) \mm\text{and}\mm m:=\sum_{\substack{k\in \Lambda\\ k\neq 0}}\bb{p_k}>0.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, for all $z\in \C$, $t\geq 0$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{L}\pr{\acc{\xi \in \T\m ;\m \bb{p(\xi)-z}^2\leq t}}\leq 14d \pr{\frac{\sqrt{\Xi}}{m}\sqrt{t}}^{\frac{1}{S}}.
    \end{equation}

