body:
[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] The process $({\bar X}^\varepsilon_t)_{t \ge 0}$ with state space $\{0,1\}$ and c\`adl\`ag  trajectories defined by 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\forall t \ge 0, \quad {\bar X}^\varepsilon_t = \sum_{k\ge 0} {\mathbf 1}_{ t \in [e_{2k+1}^{\varepsilon}, e_{2k+2}^\varepsilon )} 
\end{split}
\end{equation}
converges in law to the jump Markov process $({\bar X}_t)_{t \ge 0}$ defined in Section \ref{sec:imr}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:path_expansion_H_plus_A of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Let \(U_n(x)\) be the Chebyshev polynomial of the second kind, 
and let \(V_n,\Phi_2,\Phi_3,\underline{\Phi_2V_n},\underline{\Phi_3V_n}\) be as in Definition~(def:nonbacktracking of the paper).  Introduce
\begin{equation}
\underline{\Phi_A V_n}\;\equiv\;\sum_{i=1}^n A^i\,V_{n-i},
\end{equation}
recording that each insertion of \(A\) of total multiplicity \(i\) carries no backtracking constraint, then
\begin{equation}
U_n\bigl((H+A)/2\bigr)
=
\sum_{k\ge0}\;\sum_{\alpha\in\{2,3,A\}^k}\;\sum_{\substack{\ell_0+\cdots+\ell_k=n}} 
V_{\ell_0}
\;\underline{\Phi_{\alpha_1} V_{\ell_1}}\;\cdots\;\underline{\Phi_{\alpha_k} V_{\ell_k}},
\end{equation}
where each symbol \(\alpha_i\in\{2,3,A\}\) indicates an insertion of \(\Phi_2,\Phi_3,\Phi_A\) respectively, and the summation   runs over all nonnegative integers \(\ell_i\ge0\).

