body:
[Lemma 40 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Let $0<\xi\leq1$ and $b,d,x\in\C$. Suppose that, for some constants $c_d,C_d,C_e>0$,
        \begin{align}
                c_d\leq|d|\leq C_d,\qquad |x(b+dx)|\leq C_e\xi. \nonumber
        \end{align}
        Then
        \begin{align}
                \min\left\{|x|,\left|x+\frac bd\right|\right\}\lesssim\sqrt\xi. 
        \end{align}
        If $b\neq0$, then
        \begin{align}
                \min\left\{|x|,\left|x+\frac bd\right|\right\}\lesssim\frac{\xi}{|b|}. 
        \end{align}

