body:
[Theorem prop: duality of arXiv:2504.04792, 'Uniqueness and Longtime Behavior of the Completely Positively Correlated Symbiotic Branchi'] Let $\mu \in \mathscr{P}(C_{\text{tem}}^+ \times C_{\text{tem}}^+)$ with compact support. Let $(U^1_t, U^2_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be a solution of the martingale problem $(MP)_U$ with initial distribution $\mu$ and sample paths in $C_{C_{\text{tem}}^+ \times C_{\text{tem}}^+}[0,\infty)$. Let $\phi \in C_{\text{rap}}^+$ and let $(V_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the unique $C_{\text{rap}}^+$-valued solution of $((eq: dual of the paper))$ with $V_0 = \phi$. Then, for each $T > 0$, the following duality formula holds:
\begin{equation}

    \mathbb{E}\left[e^{-\langle X_T, \phi \rangle}\right] = \mathbb{E}\left[e^{-\langle X_0, V_T \rangle -\frac{1}{2}\int_0^T \langle V_r^2, \left(Y_{T-r} \right)^2 \rangle \mathrm{d}r}\right],
\end{equation}
where $X_t = U^1_t + U^2_t, Y_t = U^1_t - U^2_t = S_t(U^1_0 - U^2_0).$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor local curve GW g0 formula of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] (conj:GW:vertex of the paper) for $n=1$ holds if and only if
    \begin{equation}

        \GWargs{Z}{\mathsf{T}}{[\bP^1]}
        =
        \prod_{i=2}^5 \prod_{k=0}^{\deg \cL_i} \varsigma(\epsilon_i - k\epsilon_1)^{-1} \,.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 10 (Half-bridge correction) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] The updates
\begin{equation}
f_0^{(n+1)}=(\mathsf Kg_T^{(n)})^{-1},
\qquad
g_T^{(n+1)}=(\mathsf K^*f_0^{(n+1)})^{-1}
\end{equation}
are alternating KL projections onto the two marginal constraint sets and converge in Hilbert's projective metric to \((f_0,g_T)\), up to reciprocal gauge. The first factor is the source corrector omitted by a terminal-only construction. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

