[Theorem thm:second-moment of arXiv:2605.30707, 'Sharp behavior of the free energy for the two-dimensional directed polymer model'] We have the following expansion of the correlation length \(1/\mathtt{F}_2(\beta)\) in terms of the parameter \(\alpha(\beta) := \pi \frac{1+\sigma^2(\beta)}{\sigma^2(\beta)}\):
       \begin{equation*}

              {\mathtt{F}_2(\beta)} = {16}\, \mathrm{e}^{-\alpha(\beta)} \Big(1 - 4 \alpha(\beta) \mathrm{e}^{-\alpha(\beta)} + O\big( \alpha(\beta)^2 \mathrm{e}^{-2\alpha(\beta)} \big) \Big)^{-1} \qquad \text{ as } \beta \downarrow 0\,.
       \end{equation*}
       As a consequence, we have \(\mathtt{F}_2(\beta)  \sim 16\, \mathrm{e}^{-\pi}\, \mathrm{e}^{-\frac{\pi}{\sigma^{2}(\beta)}}\) as \(\beta \downarrow 0\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

