[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2609.02017, 'Optimal girth-dependent bounds for the Bethe approximation of the permanent'] The function $\varphi$ is an $\mathbf s$--$\mathbf t$ flow on
$\mc{N}$. Its value is
\begin{equation}

\operatorname{val}(\varphi)
=
\sum_{e\in E}(\mathsf J_e^+-\mathsf J_e^-)
=
\frac12\sum_{v\in V}
  (\mathsf J_v^+-\mathsf J_v^-).
\end{equation}

[Proposition 10 (Secular equation for the eigenvalues) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] If $g_j=0$ for some $j$, then $\lambda^{(N)}_j$ remains an eigenvalue of $H_{N+1}$ with eigenvector
$(u^{(N)}_j,0)$. All other eigenvalues of $H_{N+1}$ are the simple zeros of the secular function
\begin{equation}
f(z):=g_{N+1}-z-\sum_{j=1}^N \frac{|g_j^{(N)}|^2}{\lambda^{(N)}_j-z}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $3\le d\le 5$, there exists $C>0$ such that for any $R\ge 1$, $x\in \mathbb{Z}^d$, $v\in \widetilde{B}_x(R)$ and $A_1,A_2,D\subset [\widetilde{B}_x(CR)]^c$,
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{split}
			\mathbb{P}( v \xleftrightarrow{(D)} A_1, v\xleftrightarrow{(D)} A_2 )\lesssim R^{-\frac{d}{2}+1}\cdot \mathbb{P}(A_1\xleftrightarrow{(D)} A_2 ). 
		\end{split}
	\end{equation}

