[Proposition prop:height-difference-radial of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] Let $h_{\alpha\beta}$ be as in Theorem~(thm:radial-ig of the paper), and let $\eta_1$ and $\eta_2$ be two flow lines of $h_{\alpha\beta}$ with angle $\theta_1$ and $\theta_2$ started at $x_1,x_2\in\partial\mathbb{D}$. On the event $E$ where $\eta_1$ hits $\eta_2$ on its right side, 
	    we have $\mathcal{D}_{12}\in(-\pi\chi,2\lambda-\pi\chi)$. Furthermore,
	    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
	        \item If $\mathcal{D}_{12}\in(-\pi\chi,0)$, then $\eta_1$ crosses $\eta_2$ upon intersecting and does not subsequently
	cross back;
	\item If $\mathcal{D}_{12} = 0$, then $\eta_1$ merges with and does not subsequently separate from $\eta_2$ upon intersecting;
	\item If $\mathcal{D}_{12}\in(0,2\lambda-\pi\chi)$, then $\eta_1$ bounces off but does not cross $\eta_2$.
	    \end{enumerate}
	    Finally, if $\eta_1$ hits $\eta_2$ on its left, then the same result holds with $\mathcal{D}_{21} := -\mathcal{D}_{12}$ replaced with $\mathcal{D}_{12}$.

For a rotation-invariant symmetric alpha-stable-like process on R^d (d > alpha in (1,2)) and singular potential nu(dy) = sum_{n=1}^infty n^{-p} delta_{n^p}(dy), the operator -L + nu satisfies the Liouville property if and only if p <= 1 / (2 - alpha).
