[Lemma Randersimmersion of arXiv:2609.03909, 'Conic Pseudo-Finslerian Mechanical Systems'] Let $R$ be a Randers-Minkowski metric on $\mathbb R^n$ with navigation data $(h, W)$. If $V$ is a subspace, then the induced metric on $V$ is the Randers-Minkowski metric with navigation data $(\tilde h, W^{\top})$ given by
\begin{subequations}
\begin{equation*}
\tilde h := \lambda \, h\vert_{V \times V} \, ,
\end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
W^{\top} := W - W^{\perp} \, ,
\end{equation*}
\end{subequations}
where $\lambda := \frac{1}{1 - h(W^{\perp}, W^{\perp})}$ and $W^{\perp}$ is the component of $W$ $h$-orthogonal to $V$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 4 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $q \in (0,1)$, $c \in [0, q^{-1})$, $N \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $\lpplen = \{\lpplinen_{i}\}_{i \geq 1}$ be as in (\ref{Eq.Deflpplen}). We define the constants
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\sigma = \frac{q^{1/2}}{1- q}, \hspace{2mm} f = \frac{q^{1/3}}{2 (1 + q)^{2/3}},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
and the rescaled processes
\begin{equation}
\lpplenc_i(t) = \sigma^{-1} N^{-1/3} \cdot \left(\lpplinen_i(tN^{2/3}) - \frac{2qN}{1-q} - \frac{qtN^{2/3}}{1-q}\right) \mbox{ for } i \in \mathbb{N}, t \in [0,\infty).
\end{equation}

[Prop normalitycriterion of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(Y\) be a real-valued random variable.  Let \(\alpha>0\), let \((B_s)_{s\ge1}\) be a nonnegative sequence, and let \(c>0\) be some constant.  Assume that for every real \(u\) with \(S_\alpha(|u|)\ge1\),
			\begin{equation}
				|\mathbb E e(uY)|\le \exp(-cB_{S_\alpha(|u|)}).
			\end{equation}
			Assume also that
			\begin{equation}
				\sum_{s\ge1}s\exp(-cB_s)<\infty.
			\end{equation}
			Then \(Y\) is almost surely absolutely normal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma eq:1052a of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] For any $N\in\N$, $p\in[1,\infty]$ and $\mu\in(0,1]$, we denote by $\mathcal{W}^p_{N,\mu}$ the set of all time weights $u_\mu\in \mathcal{D}(\R)$ verifying
\begin{equs}
  \max_{i\leqslant N} 
    \mu^{-1/p+i}
    {\| \d^i_t u_\mu 
    \|}_{L^p((-\infty,1])}< \infty\,.
\end{equs}
Then, for every $\psi\in \mathcal{D}(\R)$, $M\geqslant N$ and $q\in[1,\infty]$, uniform in $\mu\in(0,1]$ we have
    \begin{equs}      \norm{K_{M,\mu}\big(u_\mu\psi)}_{L^{q}}&\lesssim \norm{K_{M,\mu}\psi}_{L^{q}}\,,\;\text{provided} \; u_\mu \in\mathcal{W}^\infty_{N,\mu}\,,\\
          \norm{K_{M,\mu}\big(u_\mu\psi)}_{L^{1}}&\lesssim\mu \norm{K_{M,\mu}\psi}_{L^\infty}\,,\;\text{provided} \; u_\mu \in\mathcal{W}^1_{N,\mu}\,.
    \end{equs}

