[Lemma lem:volumes of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\mathbb G=\mathbb H_X\mathbb K_X$ be the decomposition from
Definition~(def:oriented_cone_horiz of the paper). Then
\begin{align}
\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal C_e^+(\beta,\rho;X))
=
\frac{\beta^{Q-1}\rho^Q}{Q\alpha_X}
\nu_X\bigl(\mathbb B(e,1)\cap\mathbb H_X\bigr).
\end{align}
Moreover, for every $c>0$,
\begin{align}
\int_{\mathcal C_e^+(\beta,\rho;X)}
e^{-c\|g\|^2}\,dg
\geqslant
\frac{\beta^{Q-1}}{\alpha_X}
\nu_X\bigl(\mathbb B(e,1)\cap\mathbb H_X\bigr)
\int_0^\rho
r^{Q-1}e^{-c(1+\beta)^2r^2}\,dr.
\end{align}

