{"artifact_digest":"sha256:f2e3db24f44d60da7be61da0e656f73a6f1de7b874574ad88d550e2c1b7f27da","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/f2/f2e3db24f44d60da7be61da0e656f73a6f1de7b874574ad88d550e2c1b7f27da.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:962162b6aeae1816bd6785e3917c69d2cf5eac1a2b886d6ebaa0e26369165400","bundle_entry_key":"2412-01995-lemma-23-mart-prop-logsigma","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_116","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_116.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2412-01995-lemma-23-mart-prop-logsigma","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: As $g$ is the smooth solution to (equation eq:Monge of the paper), we get that
\begin{align*}\textstyle 
\log \det \Sigma_*(t,M_t)&\textstyle =-d\log(1-t)-\log\det \left(\frac{1}{2}\nabla^2 g(M_t) \right) =-d \log (1-t) -g(M_t). 
\end{align*}
Then an application of It\^{o}'s formula yields that 
\begin{align*}
    d \log \det \Sigma_*(t,M_t)=&\textstyle  \frac{d}{1-t} dt - \frac{1}{2} \sum_{i,j=1}^d \nabla^2_{ij} g(M_t)   d \langle M^i,M^j \rangle_t - \nabla g(M_t) \,dM_t \\
    =&\textstyle \frac{d}{1-t} dt-\frac{1}{2} \Tr\left(\nabla^2 g(M_t) \frac{2 (\nabla^2 g(M_t))^{-1}}{1-t} \right) dt -\nabla g(M_t) \,dM_t \\
