[Defn of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] A \textbf{generalized coarse slope} is an element of $\mathbb{R} \cup \{\pm \infty,\aleph\}$. A \textbf{generalized fine slope} is a coarse slope, plus a type in $\{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$. The meaning of $s^\heartsuit$ for $\heartsuit \in \{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$ remains the same as in \zcref{sec:T2foliations}, and we define the generalized fine slope of a $\Phi$-horizontal foliation $\mathcal{G}$ with a Reeb annulus as follows:

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\aleph^\natural$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has neither $+\infty^\sharp$ nor $-\infty^\flat$ annuli. This class was simply called $\aleph$ in the body of the article.
        \item $\aleph^\sharp$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has a $+\infty^\sharp$ annulus, but no $-\infty ^\flat$ annuli.

        \item $\aleph^\flat$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has a $-\infty^\flat$ annulus, but no $+\infty^\sharp$ annuli.

        \item $\aleph^\dagger$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has both $+\infty^\sharp$ and $-\infty^\flat$ annuli.
    \end{enumerate}
    We write $\mathscr{S}$ for the space of real fine slopes $\mathbb{R} \times \{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$, and $\widehat{\mathscr{S}}$ for the space of generalized fine slopes $(\mathbb{R} \cup \{-\infty, +\infty, \aleph\}) \times \{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$.\footnote{If preferred, $+\infty^{\sharp/\natural}$ and $-\infty^{\flat/\natural}$ may be excluded from $\widehat{\mathscr{S}}$ as they do not occur as fine slopes of $\Phi$-horizontal foliations.}

