[Lem 6. lem: uniform lower bound for random traps of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Under Assumption (1. assum: aging, random version of the paper) or (1. assum: sub-aging, random version of the paper), it holds that 
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{\delta \downarrow 0}
    \limsup_{n \to \infty}
    \mathbf{P}_{n} 
    \bigl(
      \mathsf{P}_{n}\bigl( c_{n}^{-1}\nu_{n}(B_{R_{n}}(\rho_{n}, a_{n})) < \delta \bigr) > \eta
    \bigr)
    = 0,
    \quad 
    \forall \eta > 0.
  \end{equation}

[Theorem thm:opvol of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] Let $f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ be bounded and continuous, $b:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ bounded and Lipschitz, and let
$X_{t}\in\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{sa}}$ solve
\begin{equation}
  \mathrm{d} X_{t}=b(X_{t})\,\mathrm{d} t+f(X_{t})\,\mathrm{d} S_{t}\,f(X_{t}).
\end{equation}
Then $X_{t}\in\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{sa}}$ for all $t$, and the spectral law $\mu_{t}$ satisfies, for every
polynomial $\varphi$,
writing $\mathrm{d}\eta_{t}:=f(x)^{2}\mathrm{d}\mu_{t}(x)$,
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t}\int\varphi\,\mathrm{d}\mu_{t}
  =\int\varphi'(x)b(x)\,\mathrm{d}\mu_{t}(x)
  +\frac12\iint\frac{\varphi'(x)-\varphi'(y)}{x-y}\,\mathrm{d}\eta_{t}(x)\,\mathrm{d}\eta_{t}(y),
\end{equation}
writing $\eta_{t}$ for this $f^{2}$-weighted measure to keep it distinct from the
regularised measure $\nu=\rho\boxplus\gamma_{v}$ of Lemma~(lem:regularise of the paper) and
Theorem~(thm:transition of the paper), which is a different object.
equivalently $\partial_{t}\mu_{t}+\partial_{x}(\mu_{t}V_{t})=0$ with the velocity field
\begin{equation}
  V_{t}(x)=b(x)+f(x)^{2}\,H\eta_{t}(x),
  \qquad H\eta_{t}(x)=\mathrm{p.v.}\!\int\frac{f(y)^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\mu_{t}(y)}{x-y}.
\end{equation}
For $f\equiv\sqrt\beta$ and $b(x)=-\tfrac12\beta x$ this reduces to
(equation eq:velocity of the paper).

