[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] The velocity field  defined in~\eqref{eq:def_u} satisfies
\begin{equation*}
    u \in C^{\infty}([0,1]; C^{\alpha}(\T^2))\quad \text{for any } 0< \alpha < \frac{1}{\gamma +(1-\gamma)(1+\delta)}.
\end{equation*}
In particular, for any $\alpha \in (0,1)$ and $\gamma \in (1/2,1)$ there exists $\delta \in (0,1)$ sufficiently small so that $u \in C^{\infty}([0,1]; C^{\alpha}(\T^2))$.

[Proposition 5 (Recurrence at the critical dimension for $\alpha=2$) of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] Assume that \(\alpha=2\), \emph{i.e.} \(\mu\) is attracted to a
Gaussian distribution, and that $\theta$, defined here on $\Z^4$, has a finite moment of order $\delta>4$. A \(\Tree_{n}\)-walk in \(\Z^4\) with $\theta$-jumps  is recurrent:

\begin{equation*}{
\frac{R^{\theta}(\Tree_{n})}{n} \xrightarrow[n \to +\infty]{(\P)} 0.
}\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:gradphi-UB-LD-any-point of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $1 < p < 2$, or $2 < p < \infty$. There exists $\varepsilon_\beta \to 0$ as $\beta \to \infty$ such that, for every $V \subset \mathbb Z^2$, $x \in V$, and $h$ sufficiently large compared to $\beta$,
		\begin{equation}
			{\widehat\pi}_V^{(p)}(\phi_x \geq h) \leq {\widehat\pi}_\infty^{(p)}(\phi_o \geq h)^{1 + \varepsilon_\beta}\,.
		\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:single-concentration-stable of arXiv:2411.10113, 'Long-range one-dimensional\\ internal diffusion-limited aggregation'] Suppose that~(equation ass:irreducible of the paper) holds and that~(equation ass:stable-alpha of the paper) holds with $\alpha \in (1,2)$. Take $u,s \in {\mathbb R}$, such that $1<u<s$ and let $q: = {\underline{q}_\alpha}(u,s)$ as given in equation~(equation eq:q-lower-bound of the paper).
Then, there exist $\varepsilon_0 \in (0,1)$, $K>0$, and $x_0 >0$ such that the following holds. 
For all $x>x_0$, every $\varepsilon \in (0,\varepsilon_0)$, 
with $k_x : = \lceil (q^{-1} + K\varepsilon) (s-1)x \rceil$, there is $c >0$ for which
    \begin{equation}

    \max_{t \in {\mathbb Z} \cap [ x,ux]} \Pr\left(K^+_{\sigma_x,k_x}(t,x,s)<(s-1)x\right)  \leq {\mathrm{e}}^{-c(s-1)x},
    \end{equation}
    and 
    \begin{equation}
        \max_{t \in {\mathbb Z} \cap [ x,ux]} \Pr \left( K^-_{\sigma_x,k_x}(-t,x,s)< (s-1)x\right)\leq {\mathrm{e}}^{-c(s-1)x}. 
    \end{equation}

