[Proposition 46 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $A\subset \mathbb{S}^n$ be a measurable set with positive measure. Then,
\begin{equation}
\sigma_{n}(A^s) \leq \sigma_{n}(C_A^s).

\end{equation}
If $0<\sigma_n(A) < \frac{1}{2}$, there is equality in \eqref{eq:sph_BS} if and only if $A$ is a spherical cap up to removal of null sets. If $\sigma_n(A)\geq \frac{1}{2}$, there is always equality, namely, both sides of \eqref{eq:sph_BS} are zero. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 27 of arXiv:2605.03851, 'The Relay Random Tree:\\A stochastic geometry approach of multihop relay in an urban visib'] \textbf{General Range.}

We call \textit{range} a convex compact subset $\mathrm{R}$ of $\R^ 2$ that is symmetric ($x\in R \leftrightarrow (-x)\in \R$). For $x_1, x_2$ two points of $\Half$, we say that $x_2$ of  is in range from $x_1$ if
\[x_2 \in \mathrm{R}+x_1.\]

[Proposition 1 (Heat Flow Decay) of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Let $(R_{t}, t \geq 0)$ be a diffusion semigroup, and let $\mu$ and $\nu$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assumption}. Then there exist $C > 0$ and $T_0 > 0$ (both depending on $\mu,\nu$) such that for all $t \geq T_0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \Was{2}(R_{t}^*\mu,R_{t}^*\nu) \leq C\exp(-\lambda_1 t). 
    \end{align*}

