[Thm clt:Zagreb of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] For  $m \ge 2$, as $n\to\infty$, we have
\begin{align}
    \frac{Z_n-\,{\mathbb{E}}[Z_n]}{n} \overset{d}{\longrightarrow}\sum_{i=1}^m N_i^2  -\frac{m-1}{m},
\end{align}
with $(N_1,\ldots,N_m)$ defined in (equation N_i of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] Let $T\leq\infty$. There exists a lower semicontinuous function $b_T:[0,T)\to[1/2,1]$ such that the continuation region is given by
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{C}_T=\{(t,x)\in\mathcal{S}_T : 1-b_T(t)<x<b_T(t)\}.
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, $b_T(t)\geq\gamma(t)$ for any $t\in[0,T)$.

