[Proposition 17 ({\cite[Lemma~3.3) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] {BauerHuaYau-17}}]Let $\kappa\geq 0$ and $f\in \ell^2(X,m)$. For any $\kappa$-Lipschitz function $\omega\in \cC(X)$, the function 
\begin{equation*}
\Phi:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty),\quad \ t\mapsto \exp\left(2\Lambda t -\frac{2}{S^2}\left(\cosh\left(\kappa S\right)-1\right)t\right)\ \Vert \euler^{\omega}P_tf\Vert_2^2
\end{equation*}
is non-increasing. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thmd 4 (\cite{DenRe}) of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] Let the assumptions (G) and (M) hold. Then the function
\begin{equation*}

\widehat{V}\left(\ov{x}\right):= \lim_{n \to \infty} \ex u\left(\ov{x} + \ov{S}_n\right) I\left\{ \tau(\ov{x}) > n\right\}
\end{equation*}
is well-defined and harmonic for $\left\{\ov{S}_n\right\}$ killed at leaving $K$, i.e. for every natural number $n$ and every vector $\ov{x} \in K$
\begin{equation*}

\widehat{V}\left(\ov{x}\right)= \ex \widehat{V}\left(\ov{x} + \ov{S}_n\right) I\left\{ \tau(\ov{x}) > n\right\}.
\end{equation*}
Futhermore, if $p \ge 1$, then
\begin{equation*}

\widehat{V}(\ov{x}) \sim u(\ov{x}), \;\; \mathrm{dist}\left( \ov{x}, \partial K\right) \to \infty.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

