[Corollary cor:stationary of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] In the same setting as in Theorem~(thm:main of the paper), define the projective process $ \pi_{t} =
\varrho_{t}/ \| \varrho_{t} \| $ for all $ t \geqslant 0$. Then
the couple $
(u_{t}, \pi_{t})_{t \geqslant 0} $ is a Markov process with values in $
H^{\mathbf{b}} \times S $ and there exists at least one stationary measure $\nu$ for $(u_t, \pi_t) $ on $ H^{\mathbf{b}} \times S$. Moreover any stationary measure $\nu$ satisfies for any $\mathbf{q} > 3$
\begin{equ}
\lambda_1^\kappa \geqslant - \int_{H^{\mathbf{b}} \times S} \kappa\|\nabla \pi\|^2 \mathrm{\,d}
\nu(u,\pi) \geqslant -C\kappa^{-\mathbf{q}} \;,
\end{equ}
in the case in which $L[u]$ is given by (equation e:form-PSA of the paper), and
\begin{equ}
   \lambda_1^\kappa \geqslant - \int_{H^{\mathbf{b}} \times S} \kappa\|\nabla \pi\|^2
+\langle \pi, \Delta u\cdot \nabla^{-1}\pi\rangle \mathrm{\,d} \nu(u,\pi) \geqslant
-C\kappa^{-\mathbf{q}}\;,
   \end{equ}
in the case in which $L[u]$ is given by (equation e:form-LNS of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

