[Lem 141 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] There exists $C > 1$ such that the following holds whenever $\varepsilon$ is sufficiently small. For any $q,q' \in [-\varepsilon, \varepsilon]$, we have for any $e \in [0, \mathfrak{r}_q (y)]$ that
	\begin{flalign*}
		|\partial_x \mathcal{H}_q ( \mathfrak{r}_q (y) - e, y) - \partial_x \mathcal{H}_{q'} (\mathfrak{r}_{q'} (y) - e, y) | \le C |q-q'| y^{1/4} e^{1/2}.
	\end{flalign*}

