[Prop a_k approx equation of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] On the event $A_k$ defined in Lemma (Concentration for specific functionals of theta of the paper), for $n$ sufficiently large, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]}|a_{k+1}(t)-\sqrt{n}(\theta_{k}(t)-\theta_{k-2}(t))^T\theta_{k-1}(t)| \leq C_{k,T}\frac{\log(n)^k}{\sqrt{n}},
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]}\left|b_{k+1}(t)^2-\frac{\|\theta_k(t)\|^2}{\|\theta_{k-1}(t)\|^2}\right| \leq C_{k,T}\frac{\log(n)^{2(k-1)}}{n}.
    \end{equation}

