[Theorem thm:mixing of arXiv:2412.01381, 'Ergodicity and mixing for locally monotone stochastic evolution equations'] Assume Hypotheses (hyp:hemicont of the paper),  (hyp:coerc of the paper), (hyp:coerc-g of the paper), (hyp:monotonicity of the paper), (hyp:monotonicity-g of the paper), (hyp:growth of the paper) and (hyp:regularity of the paper), (hyp:reg2 of the paper), (hyp:quant of the paper), and (hyp:mixing of the paper) hold true. Suppose that $\eta\equiv 0$ or $\rho\equiv 0$. Let $\gamma\in (0,\delta_2]$ be as in Hypothesis~(hyp:mixing of the paper).
Then for any $x\in H$ and $\varepsilon>0$ it follows that the $\varepsilon$-mixing time $\tau^x_{\textup{\textsf{mix}}}(\varepsilon)$ satisfies the following non-asymptotic estimate:
\begin{equation}
\tau^x_{\textup{\textsf{mix}}}(\varepsilon)\leq 
\frac{2}{\gamma}\left[\frac{C_2}{\lambda_0\delta_1(\beta+2)}\|x\|^{\beta+2}_H+\log\left(\|x\|_H+\left(\frac{2(c_1+c_2)}{c_0^\alpha\lambda_0\delta_1(\beta+2)}\right)^{1/(\alpha+\beta)}\right)+\log\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\right)\right].
\end{equation}

