[Lemma lem:LBI1-new of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] Consider the map $ \Phi $ as defined in (equation e:def-phi of the paper) in the case $ L
[u] = u \cdot \nabla $, and fix any $ \beta \geqslant 1 $. Then
the following estimates hold uniformly over $ \varrho_{0} \in L^{2}_{*}, \kappa \in (0, 1] $ and $M \in
\mathbf{N}_{*}, M \geqslant M^{(\beta)}(\varrho_{0}) $:
\begin{equ}
\mathbb{E} \left\| \mathcal{L}_{1} \, \Phi [ \widetilde{X}, Y]_{t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M)}
\right\|^{2} \gtrsim \kappa^{- 1} M^{ -6} \|
\varrho_{0} \|_{H^{- \frac{\mathbf{a}}{2}}}^{2} \;.
\end{equ}

