[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] For $a,b,d\in\R$ and $y\geq 0$ it holds that
\begin{equation*}
\max_{x\in[0,y]} a + bx + d(y-x)^{\frac{3}{2}} =
\begin{cases}
a + by - \frac{4}{27}\frac{b^{3}}{d^{2}}  & \text{if $d<0$, $b<0$ and $y > \frac{4}{9}\frac{b^{2}}{d^{2}}$}\\
a + \max\{b,dy^{\frac{1}{2}}\}y & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
.
\end{equation*}

