body:
[Proposition 36 of arXiv:2609.03191, 'On lifting representations and actions on curves of the metacyclic groups $C_{p^s}\rtimes '] Recall that $G=C_{p^s}\rtimes_\chi C_m$ and $q=|\Ker(\chi)|$. Let $l_1<\cdots<l_s$ (resp.\ $u_1<\cdots<u_s$) be a strictly increasing sequence of natural numbers that occur as the lower (resp.\ upper) jumps of a cyclic $C_{p^s}$-extension of $k((t))$, i.e., such that the conditions of Corollary \ref{C3}(2) (resp.\ Lemma \ref{L7}(2)) hold. Then there exists an HKG cover $X\rightarrow X/G$ with $l_1<\cdots<l_s$ (resp.\ $u_1<\cdots<u_s$) as the lower (resp.\ upper) jumps of the wild cyclic subgroup $H=C_{p^s}$ if and only if 
\begin{equation}
\gcd(m,l_1)=q\;\;\;\;\textup{and}\;\;\;\;l_i\equiv l_1\pmod m\;\;\;\forall i\in\llbracket2,s\rrbracket
\end{equation}
(resp.\ $\gcd(m,u_1)=q\;\;\;\;\textup{and}\;\;\;\;u_i\equiv u_1\pmod m\;\;\;\forall i\in\llbracket2,s\rrbracket$).

[Lemma lemma5.8 of arXiv:2411.02362, 'Limit theorems for random Dirichlet series: boundary case'] Fix sufficiently small $\delta>0$, pick $\gamma>0$ satisfying $(1+\gamma)(1-\delta^2/8)<1$ and let, as before, $\mathfrak{s}_n=\exp(-\exp(n^{1+\gamma}))$ for $n\in\mathbb{N}$. Then
\begin{equation*}
\limsup_{n\to\infty} f(\mathfrak{s}_n) \sum_{k\ge 2}\frac{(\log k)^{-1/2}}{k^{1/2+\mathfrak{s}_n}}\widetilde{\eta}_{k,1}(\mathfrak{s}_n)\ge 1-\delta\quad\text{\rm a.s.}
\end{equation*}

