[Lemma lm:PPP.clusters of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] Let $d \geq 2$ and $r>r_c$. Then, there exist $C,c>0$ such that, for each $t>0$,
    \begin{equation*}
    \mu_v\big(v \not\in \Hh , ~\mathlcal{C}(v) \not\subseteq B(v,t)\big) \leq C e^{-c t}.
    \end{equation*}
    Furthermore, there exist $C',c,>0$ and $\beta' >1$ such that, for all $u,v \in \R^d$ and every $t> \beta' \|u-v\|$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_{u,v}\big(\accentset{\rule{.4em}{.5pt}}{D}(u,v) \mathbbm{1}_{u \in\mathlcal{C}(v)}> t\big)  \leq C'e^{-c' t}.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

