{"artifact_digest":"sha256:5deea5724f1ce4960b978faf9c14afbd680152e186287bb297043ef76f93d625","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/5d/5deea5724f1ce4960b978faf9c14afbd680152e186287bb297043ef76f93d625.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1886c3a0deeb4dc0e4192eaa5fb7931b0d630adb41240ece676dc3a63c2f8a21","bundle_entry_key":"2608-31101-theorem-2-limiting-profile","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_071","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_071.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-31101-proposition-2-limiting-profile","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Write $t=\sqrt n$. From $a=1/(t+2/5)$ and (equation eq:lambda-rescue of the paper),
\begin{equation}
a=\frac1t+O(t^{-2}),
\qquad
\lambda=\frac{4}{5t^3}+O(t^{-4}).
