[Definition 11 (Transition rate) of arXiv:2506.09462, 'Transition Path Theory For L\'{e}vy-Type Processes: SDE Representation and Statistics'] The \textbf{$AB$ transition rate} \(k_{AB}\) is defined as:  
    \begin{equation*}
        k_{AB} = \lim_{T \to \infty} \frac{\mathrm{N}_T}{T},
    \end{equation*}
    which quantifies the rate of transitions from \(A\) to \(B\). Additionally, the limits:  
    \begin{equation*}
        T_{AB} := \lim_{\mathrm{N} \to \infty} \frac{1}{\mathrm{N}} \sum_{n=0}^{\mathrm{N}-1} (\tau_{B,n+1}^+ - \tau_{A,n}^+),
    \end{equation*}
    and  
    \begin{equation*}
        T_{BA} := \lim_{\mathrm{N} \to \infty} \frac{1}{\mathrm{N}} \sum_{n=0}^{\mathrm{N}-1} (\tau_{A,n+1}^+ - \tau_{B,n}^+),
    \end{equation*}
    are called the \textbf{expected transition times} from \(A \to B\) and \(B \to A\), respectively.

[Conjecture conj:quenched formula of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Define
		\begin{equation}
			\tilde{\Lambda}(\theta)=\theta\inf_{\zeta:\zeta([0,\sup(\mathrm{supp} \zeta)))=\theta}\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}(\zeta).
		\end{equation}
		Then there exists an open subset $D\subset\mathbb{R}$ such that for every $f\in D$,
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{\varepsilon\to 0}\lim_{N\to\infty}
			\frac{1}{N}\mathbb{E}\bigl[\log\mathcal{N}_\varepsilon(f)\bigr]=-\tilde{\Lambda}^*(f)=\inf_\theta \bigl(\tilde{\Lambda}(\theta)-\theta f\bigr).
		\end{equation} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

