being the roots introduced in \eqref{defP1}.

[Lemma lem:green-kernel-regularity-package of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] There exists a constant
$C_D\ge1$ such that
\begin{equation}
 0\le G_D(z,w)
 \le C_D+\log^+\frac1{|z-w|},
 \qquad z,w\in D.
\end{equation}
Away from the diagonal, the Green kernel is locally uniformly continuous in
its first variable.  More precisely, for every compact $K\Subset D$ and every
$r_\ast>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 \omega_{K,r_\ast}(\delta)
 &:=\sup_{\substack{z,z'\in K,\ |z-z'|\le\delta\\
                    w\in D,\ |z-w|\ge r_\ast,\ |z'-w|\ge r_\ast}}
    |G_D(z,w)-G_D(z',w)|,
    \qquad \delta>0,\\
 \omega_{K,r_\ast}(\delta)
 &\xrightarrow[\delta\downarrow0]{}0.
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}

[Lem 18 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d \geq 2$.  
	There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $G$ subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$, every $\beta\geq \beta_c/2$, every $x\in V(G)$ and $zw\in E(G)$, 
\begin{equation}
	\frac{1}{C}\langle \sigma_x \sigma_w \rangle_{G, \beta} \leq \langle \sigma_x \sigma_z \rangle_{G, \beta} \leq  C \langle \sigma_x \sigma_w \rangle_{G, \beta}.
\end{equation}
Similarly, for any $\mathsf{h}\in (\mathbb{R}^+)^V$ and $zw \in E(G)$,
	\begin{equation}
		\langle \sigma_z \rangle_{G, \beta, \mathsf{h}} \leq C \langle \sigma_w \rangle_{G, \beta, \mathsf{h}}
	\end{equation}

