{"artifact_digest":"sha256:9aa608755fffaef77fc9138d04cf9e665899d1c449c6c4a285a10f57337e1767","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/9a/9aa608755fffaef77fc9138d04cf9e665899d1c449c6c4a285a10f57337e1767.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:7f242e3c8112aab31e2e007fa027c43df9e9385c58933276baa2db19a179a0fd","bundle_entry_key":"2605-05864-lemma-22-pot-lem","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_027","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_027.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-05864-lemma-22-pot-lem","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: By \cite[Proposition 7.1.1.e]{F99}, for a non-negative lower semi-continuous function \(f\), it holds that
\[\int_E f \,d\mu = \sup{\left\{\int_E \varphi\,d\mu : \varphi \in C_c, 0\leq \varphi \leq f\right\}}.\]
For \(\varphi \in C_c\) satisfying \(0\leq \varphi \leq f\), we have
\begin{eqnarray*}
