\end{equation}

Henceforth, fix $f=(uv)$ and write $u'\ne u$ and $v'\ne v$. 
Let $\mathcal{P}_{uv}$ denote the set of $P\in \mathcal{P}_S$ for which $p_{2,v}<p_{1,u'}$.
Since $p_{2,v}$ and $p_{1,u'}$ are independent with the same probability density function
