Using part (ii) of Theorem (Thm_MakNikPal of the paper) with the choices $x:=x_i$, $i=1,\ldots,n$, and $x_0:=\sum_{i=1}^n t_ix_i$, we have that
 \begin{align*}
  L(x_i)\geqslant L(x_0) + c_{x_0}(x_i-x_0) + \alpha(x_i-x_0),\qquad i=1,\ldots,n,
 \end{align*}
where $c_{x_0}\in\mathbb{R}$.
Multiplying this inequality by $t_i$, $i=1,\ldots,n$, and summing up the corresponding inequalities side by side, we can obtain that
 \begin{align*}
   \sum_{i=1}^n t_iL(x_i)
     \geqslant L(x_0) + c_{x_0}\sum_{i=1}^n t_i(x_i-x_0)
        + \sum_{i=1}^n t_i \alpha(x_i-x_0),
 ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:395aab59843d610d0cff8c619d4ceb7d490640b2e1a1bcbc9d6ba8f469746b44","revision_digest":"sha256:657da6e8e2b2315c6dc6b9fa015636b3b4274fb2294211bb6cf4251015744a90","source_id":"arxiv:2606.22183","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

