[Lem exs thT of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exists a constant $a_3 \in (0,1)$ such that, for any $x \in M$ and $t>0$,
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{\delta \downarrow 0}
    \hat{P}_{\diag(x)}
    \left(
      \sigma^{\mathrm{G}}(\delta;a_3) \leq t
    \right)
    =
    1.
  \end{equation}

[Lem lower-bound-prob of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}_{0}}$ and $(X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}_{0}}$ are independent sequences of exponential random variables, with $X_{i} \sim X'_{i} \sim \exponentialrv\left( f(i) \right)$. Suppose, moreover, that $n, \phi_{n} \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$ are given such that
    $n < \phi_{n} - 1$, and  
    \begin{equation} 
    \frac{3\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \frac{1}{f(i)}\right)^2}{\sum_{i=n}^{\phi_{n} - 1} \frac{1}{f(j)^2}} \leq \frac{1}{2}.
    \end{equation}
    Then, 
    \begin{equation} 
        \Prob{\sum_{i=1}^{\phi_{n} - 1} X_{i} < \sum_{i=n}^{\phi_{n}-1} X'_{i}} > \frac{1}{176}. 
    \end{equation}

