  (ass:standing of the paper) with \(r\geqslant 2\). Let \(A>0\). There exists \(\sigma_0>0\) and a function
  \(\mathscr E_{\mathrm{in}}\) from the class \(\mathfrak B_{r-2}\) on \(\mathcal D_{A,\mathcal{K}_{
  \mathcal{S}}, \sigma_0}\) such that
  \begin{align}
    I_\sigma(a,x) &= \mathsf C_0(a,x) + \sigma\mathsf C_1(a,x)
    + \sigma^2\mathscr E_{\mathrm{in}}(a,x,\sigma) \notag \\
    &\qquad + \operatorname{Tail}_{\mathrm{ex}}(a,x,\sigma) - \operatorname{Tail}_{0}(a,x,\sigma)
    - \sigma\operatorname{Tail}_{1}(a,x,\sigma). 
  \end{align}

[Lemma l:dis of arXiv:2604.03979, 'Stationary Distributions in Monotone Markov Models: Theory and Applications'] For all $\epsilon > 0$, there exists a $\tau \in \mathbb T$ such that

    \begin{equation}
        s,t \in \mathbb T \text{ with }  \tau \leq s,t
        \quad \implies \quad
        d(T_s \, \bar x, T_t \, \bar x) < \epsilon .
    \end{equation}

