[Lem ;laltu of arXiv:2604.12462, 'Stochastic analysis of Beckner's and related functional inequalities'] We have 
\begin{align}
 U(z)=C_{p}'\int _{0}^{z}du\,\int _{0}^{u}dv\,\int _{0}^{\infty }d\lambda  \,\lambda  ^{\nua +2}
 K_{\nua }(\lambda  )\exp \!\left\{ 
 -\frac{(p-1)^{2}v}{2}\lambda  ^{2}
 \right\} 
\end{align}
for all $z\ge 0$. Here the constant $C_{p}'$ is given by 
\begin{align*}
 C_{p}'=\frac{2^{\frac{1}{2(p-1)}}}{\sqrt{\pi }\Gamma \Bigl( 
 \frac{3p-4}{2(p-1)}
 \Bigr) }
\end{align*}
and $K_{\nua }$ is the modified Bessel function of the third kind 
(or Macdonald's function) of order $\nua $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop proba ineq decoupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $W$ be a measurable set of $\mathcal W_{T_1}\times \mathcal W_{T_2}$ and let 
	\begin{equation*}
		U=\{u\in \widetilde{\mathcal{W}}_n\ |\ \Phi_{n,T_1,T_2}(u)\subseteq W\}.
	\end{equation*}
	Then,
	\begin{equation}

		\mathbb P (U)\leqslant (n+1)^{2r+1}(\tau_K+1)^rc_K^r\mathbb P^{\otimes 2}(W).
	\end{equation}

[Proposition prop: 1wr fixed n of arXiv:2507.04505, 'Heights of butterfly trees'] Let $\pi \sim \operatorname{Unif}(S_n \wr S_m)$ or $\pi \sim \operatorname{Unif}(S_m \otimes S_n)$, and $h_{n,m} = h(\mathcal T(\pi))$. Then for any $\varepsilon>0$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{m \to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left({h_{n,m}} \ge (c^* H_n^{(1)}-\varepsilon)\log m\right) = 1.
    \end{equation*}

[Corollary cor uniform exploration from x of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] Jointly with the convergences~(equation eq cv subsequence of the paper) and~(equation eq cv Hausdorff ball of the paper), along a subsequence which is again denoted by $(\kappa_n)_{n \ge 0}$,
	\begin{equation}
		\left( \SCB_{\ka_{\kappa_n}t}^{\kappa_n,\partial}( \SCL^{\kappa_n}(x))\right)_{t \in \BQ_{\ge 0}, x \in \BQ^2}
		\mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits_{n\to \infty}^{(\mathrm{d})}
		\left( \SCB_t^\partial( \SCL(x))\right)_{t \in \BQ_{\ge 0}, x \in \BQ^2}
	\end{equation}
	for the product topology in $x \in \BQ^2$ and $t \in \BQ_{\ge 0}$, where the space of compact sets is equipped with the Hausdorff topology, and where $(\SCB^\partial_t(\SCL(x)))_{t\ge 0}$ has the law of the explored region in the uniform exploration of the $\CLE_4$ started from $\SCL(x)$ (where the time parametrization is that of the PPP of SLE bubbles).

[Theorem thm:unique-opt of arXiv:2608.22765, 'Learning to Control Coupled-Dynamics Environments with Joint Markov Decision Processes'] Under Condition~(cond:unique-opt of the paper), for any $p\ge1$ and $\eta_0\in\mathcal E_p$, the iterates $\eta_{k+1}=\mathcal T_G\eta_k$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
D_p(\eta_k,\eta^{\pi^*}_{\mathcal H})\to0.
\end{equation}
In particular, $W_p(\eta_k(h_s),\eta^{\pi^*}_{\mathcal H}(h_s))\to0$ for every $s$.

