[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2605.31300, 'Cone-Additive Functions for Random Walks on Free Products of Graphs'] Assume that $f:\Pi\to\mathbb{R}$ is a cone-additive function such that there exist  constants $C\in(0,\infty)$ and $R\in(0,\mathcal{R})$ with 
\begin{equation*} 
 \bigl|f(\pi)\bigr| \leq C\cdot R^{\mathrm{length}(\pi)} \quad \textrm{ for all } \pi\in\Pi.
\end{equation*}
Then:
$$
\lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{f\bigl(\pi^\ast_n\bigr)}{n}=0 \quad \textrm{almost surely.}
$$

