body:
[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] For any $\eta\in (0,1)$ and $\epsilon>0$,
		\begin{align*}
			&\limsup_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{1}{\mu(t)}\int_{\Omega'_\epsilon}\P_x\left(\inf_{0\le s\le t}\phi(X_s)\le 0\right)dx \\
			&\le \sup_{0\le v\le \epsilon}\mathcal{H}^{d-1}(\partial\Omega_v)\frac{M_\epsilon}{\eta m_\epsilon}+ 2\sup_{0\le v\le \epsilon}\mathcal{H}^{d-1}(\partial\Omega_v)\frac{(1-\eta)^{-\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+1}}}{m_\epsilon} \epsilon^{\frac{\kappa}{\kappa+1}},
		\end{align*} 
		where $M_\epsilon=\sup_{x\in \Omega'_\epsilon} |\nabla \phi(x)|$ and $m_\epsilon=\inf_{x\in \Omega'_\epsilon} |\nabla \phi(x)|$.

