body:
[Proposition claim:moment expansion of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Let $X_1,\ldots,X_n$ be Bernoulli random variables and let $X=\sum_{i=1}^{n} X_i$. Suppose that for any subset of indices $S\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}$ with $\abs{S}\leq 4$, there is a constant $\widetilde C$ such that

    \ben{
        \mathbb{P} \left( X_i = 1 \text{ for all } i \in S \right) \leq \widetilde C \prod_{i \in S} \mathbb{P} (X_i = 1).
    }
 Then there is a constant $\widehat C$ depending only on $\widetilde C$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{E} \left[ X^4 \right] \leq \widehat C \bclr{\mathbb{E}[X]+\mathbb{E}[X]^4}.

    \end{align*}

