[Lemma lemma_basis_L^2 of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Let us denote by $\nu^N_\alpha$ the Bernoulli product measure in $ {\{0,1\}^{\Sigma^-_l}}$ of parameter $\alpha \in (0,1)$. Denote, for every $x \in  {\Sigma^-_l}$, the $L^2(\nu_\alpha^N)$ functions
\begin{equation*}
    v_x(\eta) := \frac{\eta(x)-\alpha}{\alpha(1-\alpha)},
\end{equation*}
where $\eta \in  {\{0,1\}^{\Sigma^-_l}}$. Then, $\{v_x \ | \ x \in  {\Sigma^-_l}\}$ is an orthonormal basis of $L^2(\nu_\alpha^N)$.
In particular,
 {$\{\eta^{k_1}(\epsilon_N)\dots\eta^{k_l}(l\epsilon_N): k_j \in \{0,1\}, j \in \{1,\dots,l\}, \eta \in  {\{0,1\}^{\Sigma^-_l}}\}$} generates $L^2(\nu_\alpha^N)$ {, where here $\eta^{k_j}(z)$ represents $1$ if $k_j=0$ and $\eta(z)$ if $k_j=1$, for every $z \in  {\Sigma^-_l}$.}

