[Corollary c:purejumppareto of arXiv:2604.03979, 'Stationary Distributions in Monotone Markov Models: Theory and Applications'] Let $h \equiv x_0$, $\nu = \delta_0$, and $\mu =
    \mathrm{Exp}(\theta)$ for some $\theta > 0$. In this setting, for the income
    level $Y = e^X$, the tail of the unique stationary distribution is Pareto:
    for $y > y_0 \coloneq e^{x_0}$,

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P(Y > y)
        = q \left(\frac{y}{y_0}\right)^{-\alpha}
        \quad \text{with} \quad
        \alpha \coloneq \frac{\lambda_2 \theta}{\lambda_1 + \lambda_2}.
    \end{equation}

[Lemma lem:wp:marginalSDE of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:lyapunov of the paper) and $(\mu, \gamma, \mathbf{X})$ is a linear growth solution to $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, T]$ with potentials $(U, W)$  and initial condition $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$. Then for all $t \in [0, T]$, the edge time marginal $\bar{\mu}_t$ satisfies $\bar{\mu}_t = \mathcal{L}(\bar{X}_0(t), \bar{X}_1(t))$, where $(\bar{X}_0, \bar{X}_1)$ solve the following SDE with initial condition $\bar{\lambda}$:
        \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            d{\bar{X}}_0(t) &= \gamma(t, \bar{X}_0(t), \bar{X}_1(t)) dt + \sqrt{2}d\tilde{B}_0(t), \\
            d{\bar{X}}_1(t) &= \gamma(t, \bar{X}_1(t), \bar{X}_0(t)) dt + \sqrt{2}d\tilde{B}_1(t), 
                    \end{aligned}

    \end{equation}
    where $\tilde{B}_0, \tilde{B}_1$ are independent $d$-dimensional Brownian motions. Moreover, we have
    \begin{equation*}
    \int_0^T \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d \times \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d} \frac{|\nabla_{(x_0, x_1)} \bar{\mu}_t(x_0, x_1)|^2}{\bar{\mu}_t(x_0, x_1)} dx_0 dx_1 dt < \infty.
\end{equation*}

