body:
[Proposition 75 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mu_1$ and $\mu_2$ be positive premeasures such that $\q{\mu_1} = \q{\mu_2}$, $\eta_1 = \as[\mf R]{\mu_1}$, and $\eta_2 = \as[\mf R]{\mu_2}$.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item [(i)] $\as[\mf R]{\mu_1\dotplus_\R \mu_2} = \eta_1 \dotplus_{\mf R} \eta_2$. 
  \item [(ii)] $\mu_1 \dotleq_\R \mu_2$ if and only if  $\eta_1\dotleq_{\mf R}\eta_2$.
  \end{enumerate}

