[Lemma lem:opposite of arXiv:2609.03448, 'Prime-power Diophantine tuples'] Let $a<b<c<d$ belong to a reduced $D(\varepsilon N)$-tuple and write
\[
\begin{array}{lll}
 ab+\varepsilon N=x_1^2,&ac+\varepsilon N=x_2^2,&bc+\varepsilon N=x_3^2,\\
 ad+\varepsilon N=x_4^2,&bd+\varepsilon N=x_5^2,&cd+\varepsilon N=x_6^2.
\end{array}
\]
Assume that every triple among $a,b,c,d$ is in the $\bar e$-branch.  Then
\begin{equation}
 x_1x_6\equiv x_2x_5\equiv x_3x_4\pmod N.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that Assumptions {\rm\ref{A1}}, {\rm\ref{A2}}, {\rm\ref{A3}} and  {\rm\ref{A4}} hold.
For any $x\in\RR^{n}$, the SDE \eqref{e:ASDE1} has a unique strong solution $(\bar{X}_t)_{t\ge0}$. Moreover, for any $p\ge 2$ and $T>0$, there exists a constant $C_{p,T}>0$ such that
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\left(\sup_{t\in [0, T]}|\bar{X}_{t}|^{p}\right)\le  C_{p,T}(1+|x|^{p}),
\end{align}
and, for any $h>0$ with $0\le  t<t+h\le  T$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}|\bar X_{t+h}-\bar X_{t}|^{2}
\le  C_{T}\left(1+|x|^{2}\right) h.
\end{align}

