[Theorem thm5.1' of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] The reflected BSDE (equation eq7' of the paper) has a unique solution $(\{Y^i,Z^i\}_{1\leq i\leq N},K^{(N)})$ with $K^{(N)}\in \mathcal{A}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$, $Y^i\in \mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$ and $Z^i\in \mathcal{H}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)};\mathbb{R}^N)$ for $i=1,\cdots,N$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
    \mathsf{E}\left[|K^{(N)}_T|^2\right]\leq C.
\end{align*}

[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.15843, 'Long-time behaviour of DLRA for SDEs'] Suppose Assumptions~(H1)--(H5) hold, and let $(U_t,Y_t)_{t\ge0}$ be the solution of Eqn.~\eqref{eq:DO} with initial condition $U_0 \in V_r(\bb R^d)$ and $Y_0 \in L^2(\Omega,\bb R^r)$. Assume further that there exists $\sigma_{Y_0} > 0$ such that $\bb E[Y_0 Y_0^\top] \succeq \sigma_{Y_0} I_r$.
For any $Q\in O(r)$, define $\al R_Q(u,y) := (Qu, Qy)$. Then, for any $t>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \scr L_{(U_t^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)},Y_t^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)})}=\scr L_{(QU_t^{(U_0,Y_0)},QY_t^{(U_0,Y_0)})},
\end{equation}
where $(U_0^{(U_0,Y_0)},Y_0^{(U_0,Y_0)})=(U_0,Y_0)$ and $(U_0^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)},Y_0^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)})=(QU_0,QY_0)$.

[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2608.29736, '2608.29736'] Let $(M^n,\omega)$ be a compact K\"ahler manifold of complex
 dimension $n\geq 2$. Let $\chi$ be another K\"ahler form. Suppose that the $J$-semistable condition~\eqref{topintegralnonnegative}--~\eqref{$J$-semistablecondition} holds.
Then for any modified nef class $\beta$, we have \begin{equation}
    \int_M F_{n-1}(\chi)\wedge\beta \geq c\int_M \omega^{n-1}\wedge \beta,
    \end{equation}
    where \begin{equation}
   c= \frac{2n\displaystyle\int_M\Big(\chi^n-n\chi^{n-1}\wedge\omega\Big)+\int_M \omega^n}{8n^2\displaystyle\int_M\chi\wedge\omega^{n-1}}.\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 15 (Block-pairing principle) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $k_i=[k_{i,n}]\in\cK_{s_i}$, $1\le i\le m$, and
$\ell_j=[\ell_{j,n}]\in\cK_{t_j}$, $1\le j\le \ell$, with
$\sum_i s_i=\sum_jt_j=q$.  Then
\begin{align}
 &\Ulim q!\ip{\Sym\bigotimes_i k_{i,n}}
                     {\Sym\bigotimes_j\ell_{j,n}}
 \notag\\
 &\qquad=
 \1_{\{m=\ell\}}
 \sum_{\substack{\pi\in\mathfrak S_m\\s_i=t_{\pi(i)}}}
 \prod_{i=1}^m
 \ip{k_i}{\ell_{\pi(i)}}_{\cK_{s_i}}.

\end{align}
Here
\begin{equation}
 \ip{k_i}{\ell_j}_{\cK_s}
 =s!\,\Ulim\ip{k_{i,n}}{\ell_{j,n}},

\end{equation}
so the full multiplicity $\prod_i s_i!$ of the matched internal legs is
already contained in the right-hand side.

[Lemma lem:third-psa of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] Consider the map $ \Phi $ as in (equation e:def-phi of the paper) with $ L [u] = u \cdot \nabla $.
For any $ 1 < \alpha  < \mathbf{a}/2 $, we can estimate uniformly
over $ \kappa \in (0, 1] $:
\begin{equ}
\mathbb{E} \bigl\| \mathcal{L}_{1}  \bigl[  \Pi^{(1)}
\Phi[X,\Phi[X,\Phi[X, Y]]]_{t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M)} \bigr] \bigr\|^{2}\lesssim (t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M))^{5} \kappa^{-2} \| \varrho_{0}
\|_{H^{- \alpha}}^{2} (\| u_{0} \|^{4}_{\mathcal{C}^{\alpha}}+1)\;.
\end{equ}

[Question q:density of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Does
\[
 \frac{|\mathcal R(h,4)|}
 {|[3h+1,\binom{h+3}{3}]\cap\mathbb Z|}
\]
have a limit?  If so, is the limit equal to $1$? (Stated as a question by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

