[Definition def:VDC of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] An open set $\Omega\subset\mathbb{G}$ is said to satisfy the \emph{volume density condition} if there exists $c>0$ such that for all $r>0$ and $x\in\partial\Omega$,
    \begin{align*}
        \operatorname{Vol}(\overline{\Omega}^c\cap \mathbb{B}(x,r))\geqslant c r^Q,
    \end{align*}
    where $Q$ is the homogeneous dimension of $\mathbb{G}$.

For integers 2 <= s <= t, every simple bipartite graph G with part sizes m and n containing no subgraph isomorphic to K_{s, t} (with s vertices in the part of size m) has at most z(m, n; s, t) <= (s - 1)^{1/t} (m - s + 1) n^{1 - 1/t} + (t - 1) m edges. In particular, for m = n, ex(n, K_{s,t}) = O(n^{2 - 1/s}).
G is bipartite with parts m, n
G contains no K_{s,t}

[Defi eq:w gap of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For $p\geq 1$  and  $\Pi_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}( \mathsf{S})$, $i=0,1$, 
define 
\begin{align}
   \mathscr W_{gap,p}^p(\Pi_0,\Pi_1):=\inf_{\mathsf U\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_s(\Pi_0,\Pi_1)}\int \left\lvert \mathsf{s}_1- \mathsf{s}'_1\right\rvert^p\mathsf U(d \mathsf{s},d \mathsf{s}').
\end{align}

[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2609.02175, '2609.02175'] Assume \eqref{eq:radial-short-range},
	\eqref{eq:radial-keller}, \eqref{eq:radial-energy}, and
	\eqref{eq:radial-convexity}. Then the deflection function
	$b\mapsto\Theta_\lambda(b)$ is strictly decreasing:
	\begin{equation}
		\Theta_\lambda'(b)<0,
		\qquad b>0.
	\end{equation}
	Moreover,
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{b\to0^+}\Theta_\lambda(b)=\pi,
		\qquad
		\lim_{b\to+\infty}\Theta_\lambda(b)=0.
	\end{equation}
	In particular, for every scattering angle
	$\Theta\in(0,\pi)$, there exists a unique impact parameter
	$b>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\Theta_\lambda(b)=\Theta.
	\end{equation}

