body:
[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.06646, 'Three-dimensional stochastic wave equation with non-Lipschitz coefficients'] Given a positive integer $N$, let $A,B_i\ge 0$ and $k_i>-1$ for $i=1,2,\dots,N$. Assume that the real valued function $f: [0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ is non-negative which satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        f(t)\le A+\int_0^t\lr{\sum_{i=1}^N B_i(t-s)^{k_i}}f(s)\ud s\,,\quad\text{for all $t>0$.}
    \end{equation}
    Then, it holds that
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{t\in[0,T]}f(t)\le 2A e^{\beta t}\,,
    \end{align*}
    for all $T\ge 0$ and $\beta\ge \max\bigl\{\lr{2NB_i\Gamma(k_i+1)}^{\frac{1}{k_i+1}}\vee 1:i=1,\dots,N\bigr\}$.

