[Defn d:stabilizing-graph of arXiv:2605.28430, 'Limit theory for Lipschitz-localized statistics in random geometric models'] We say that a family of graphs 
    $(\Psi(\mathcal{P}_n))_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$  (where each graph is generated by the same rule \(\mu \mapsto \Psi(\mu)\) represented by the marking neighborhood $\bar N$) forms a {\em stabilizing interaction graph} \(\Psi\) on finite windows with respect to a point process \(\mathcal{P}\) if   for every \(p \in \mathbb{N}\), there exist a fast decreasing function $\varphi_p'$ (see~(equation varphibd of the paper)), such that the  interaction range satisfies:
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{1 \leq n < \infty} \sup_{x_1, \ldots, x_p \in W_n} \mathbb{P}_{\bk x1p}
\bigl(S_n(x_1, \mathcal{P}_n) > s\bigr) \leq \varphi_p'(s), \quad s > 0.
\end{equation}
Without loss of generality, we assume that $\varphi_p'(\cdot)\le \varphi_{p+1}'(\cdot)$ for $p \in \mathbb{N}$.

[Theorem thm:results:convergence of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption  (as:results:strongCoercivity of the paper) and Assumption (as:results:fixedPoint of the paper), and $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ satisfy $\mathbb{H}_\kappa(\lambda) < \infty$.       Let $(\mu, \gamma)$ be a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, \infty)$ with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\lambda$.
      Then we have
    \begin{equation}

        \lim_{t \rightarrow \infty}d_{LP}(\mu_t, \mathcal{S}_\kappa) = 0,
    \end{equation}
    where $d_{LP}$ is the Levy-Prokhorov metric. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 68 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is countably ($r$-)monotonically complete;
\item[(ii)] Every countable directed dominable subset of $\Ba_{F_{+}}$ has a supremum in $F$ (of norm at most $r$);
\item[(iii)] $F$ is norm complete and every countable disjoint $D\subset F_{+}$ such that $D^{\vee}\subset\Ba_{F}$ has a supremum in $F$ (of norm at most $r$);
\item[(iv)] The sequential order adherence of $\Ba_{F}$ in $F^{u}$ is contained in $F$ (in $r\Ba_{F}$);
\item[(v)] Every uo-Cauchy sequence in $\Ba_{F}$ has a uo-limit (of norm at most $r$).\medskip

In particular, $F$ is countably monotonically complete and $\sigma$-semicontinuous if and only if $\Ba_{F}$ is sequentially complete with respect to uo convergence.

[Lemma eq:linear-stat-uniform of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:GOE-linear-stat}
Let \(f\in\mathcal F_m\), or let \(f=\ell_\eta\) for a fixed \(\eta>0\), and
define
\[
 L_{N,f}(u)=\operatorname{Tr} f(\gamma_{N,p}M_n-puI_n).
\]
For every compact \(K\subset\mathbb R\),
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{u\in K}\left|
 \frac1N\log\mathbb E e^{L_{N,f}(u)}-\ell_{p,f}(u)
 \right|\longrightarrow0.
\end{equation}
Moreover, uniformly in \(u\in\mathbb R\),
\begin{equation}
 \frac1N\log\mathbb E e^{L_{N,f}(u)}
 \le
 \begin{cases}
  \left\lVertf\right\rVert_\infty,&f\in\mathcal F_m,\\
  C_{p,\eta}+\log(2+\left\lvertu\right\rvert),&f=\ell_\eta.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}

