body:
[Definition of arXiv:2412.01995, 'Exciting games and Monge-Amp\`{e}re equations'] A convex function $u_1: [0,1) \times \Delta \to \mathbb R$ is said to be a viscosity sub-solution to (equation eq:gHJB of the paper) if 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] For any $x_0 \in \Delta$, $\limsup_{(t,x) \to (1,x_0)} u_1(t,x) \leq 0$. 
    \item[(ii)] For any convex test function $\phi \in C^2([0,1) \times \Delta; \mathbb R)$, and any local maximum $(t_0,x_0) $ of $u_1 - \phi$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        -\partial_t \phi(t_0,x_0) \leq H(t_0, u_1(t_0,x_0), \det \nabla^2 \phi(t_0,x_0)).
    \end{align*}
\end{enumerate}
A convex function $u_2: [0,1) \times \Delta \to \mathbb R$ is said to be a viscosity super-solution to (equation eq:gHJB of the paper) if 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] For any $x_0 \in \bar{\Delta}$, $\liminf_{(t,x) \to (1,x_0)} u_2(t,x) \geq 0$. 
    \item[(ii)] For any $(t_0,x_0) \in [0,1) \times \partial \Delta$, $\liminf_{(t,x) \to (t_0,x_0)} u_2(t,x)=+\infty$
    \item[(iii)] For any convex test function $\phi \in C^2([0,1) \times \Delta; \mathbb R)$, and any local minimum $(t_0,x_0)$ of $u_2 - \phi$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        -\partial_t \phi(t_0,x_0) \geq H(t_0, u_2(t_0,x_0), \det \nabla^2 \phi(t_0,x_0)).
    \end{align*}
\end{enumerate}
A continuous function $u: [0,1) \times \Delta \to \mathbb R$ is said to be a viscosity solution to (equation eq:gHJB of the paper) if it is a sub-solution and super-solution.

