[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2609.03793, 'Typical martingale diverges on a co-$\sigma$-porous set'] Let $\varphi\colon\N\ra\R^+$ be a decreasing function such that $\varphi(n)\ra0$ and
\begin{equation}

\forall q>0\forall n_0\in\N\exists n\geq n_0:\varphi(n+1)<q\cdot\varphi(n).
\end{equation}
Also, let us consider any $\es\neq A\subset2^\N$. Then $A$ is not porous in $(2^\N,\psi_\varphi)$.

