[Lem head-controls of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] Let $1\ler_{\star}\le d$, let $A\in\operatorname{rip}(\delta,k)$
with $\delta<\delta_{\mathrm{sharp}}(k/r_{\star})$, and let $\lambda>\lambda_{0}\ge0$.
 Suppose $\sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$ satisfies 
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{2}\normtwo{A\sigma}^{2}+\lambda\bigl(\normone{\sigma_{\mathrm{tail}}}-\normone{\sigma_{\mathrm{head}}}\bigr)\le\lambda_{0}\normone{\sigma}.
\end{equation}
Then \begin{subequations}
\begin{align}
\mathsf{D} & \le\frac{2\lambda_{0}}{\lambda-\lambda_{0}}\mathsf{H},\\
\normtwo{A\sigma}^{2} & \le2(\lambda+\lambda_{0})\sqrt{r_{\star}}\,\mathsf{H},\\
\normtwo{\sigma} & \le\sqrt{2+\frac{2\lambda_{0}}{\lambda-\lambda_{0}}}\,\mathsf{H}.
\end{align}
\end{subequations} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

