[Lem lower-bound-prob-2 of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Assume Assumption~(ass:non-persistence of the paper) is satisfied, with $C' > 0$ satisfying Item~(item:non-persistence-two of the paper) of Assumption~(ass:non-persistence of the paper). Suppose that $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ and $(X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ are independent sequences of random variables, with $X_{i} \sim X'_{i}$. Suppose, moreover, that $n, \phi_{n} \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$ are given such that
    $n < \phi_{n} - 1$, and  
    \begin{equation} 
    \frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \E{X_{i}}\right)^2}{\sum_{i=n}^{\phi_{n} - 1} \var{X_{i}}} \leq \frac{1}{2}.
    \end{equation}
    Then, 
    \begin{equation} 
        \Prob{\sum_{i=1}^{\phi_{n} - 1} X_{i} < \sum_{i=n}^{\phi_{n}-1} X'_{i}} > \frac{1}{96 + 4C'}. 
    \end{equation}

