[Lem opt-is-path-length of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] Define the sequence $(\Psi_n)_{n≥0}$ recursively as
    \begin{equation}
        \Psi_n := \Ek*{\sum_{i=0}^K \Psi_{I^{(i)}_n} + I^{(i)}_nh_{\mathrm{opt}}(i)},
    \end{equation}
    with $\Psi_n := 0$ for $n≤ K$.
    Then, there is a constant $\widehat \beta_K\in \mathbb{R}$, such that
    \begin{equation*}

        \Psi_n
        = \frac{\gamma_K}{H_{K+1}-1} n\ln n + \widehat \beta_K n + o(n).
    \end{equation*}

